(window.LINGUA_BOOK=window.LINGUA_BOOK||{}).condense=Object.assign(window.LINGUA_BOOK.condense||{},{"part-011-chapter-11-child-language-acquisition":{"title":{"en":"Chapter 11: Child Language Acquisition","zh":"第 11 章：儿童语言习得"},"summary":{"en":"This chapter examines how children build the components of mental grammar: phonetics, phonology, morphology, syntax and semantics. It argues that children acquire grammar very quickly whenever other language users are available to observe, and it sets out the milestones, experimental methods, signed-language parallels and bilingual benefits covered in the chapter ahead.","zh":"本章考察儿童如何建立心理语法的各个组成部分：语音学、音位学、形态学、句法与语义学。儿童只要身边有可供观察的语言使用者，就能迅速习得语法；本章据此列出语言发展里程碑、实验方法、手语与口语的平行发展，以及双语习得的益处与要点。"},"points":[{"en":"Children develop phonetics, phonology, morphology, syntax and semantics as parts of mental grammar.","zh":"儿童把语音学、音位学、形态学、句法与语义学各部分发展为心理语法。"},{"en":"Children acquire grammar quickly as long as other language users are available to observe.","zh":"只要身边有可供观察的语言使用者，儿童习得语法的速度就很快。"},{"en":"Learners will identify typical language development milestones from acquisition data.","zh":"学习者将能依据习得数据辨认典型的语言发展里程碑。"},{"en":"Experimental methods reveal what children's mental grammars contain at each stage.","zh":"实验方法可以揭示儿童各阶段心理语法的内容。"},{"en":"Signed language development parallels spoken language when an accessible environment is available.","zh":"在有可及语言环境时，手语发展与口语发展相互平行。"}],"terms":[{"en":"mental grammar","zh":"心理语法","defEn":"The system of linguistic knowledge stored in a speaker's mind.","defZh":"说话者头脑中存储的语言知识系统。"},{"en":"acquisition","zh":"习得","defEn":"The natural development of grammar without explicit instruction.","defZh":"无需明确教学而自然形成语法的过程。"},{"en":"milestone","zh":"里程碑","defEn":"A typical stage that children reach in language development.","defZh":"儿童在语言发展中通常达到的阶段。"}],"examples":[],"body":[{"en":"This chapter traces how children assemble the components of mental grammar: phonetics, phonology, morphology, syntax and semantics. Each component is examined through acquisition data rather than adult descriptions. The guiding claim is that children's minds are equipped to acquire grammar very quickly, provided they have other language users to observe.","zh":"本章追踪儿童如何构建心理语法的各个组成部分：语音学、音位学、形态学、句法与语义学。每一部分都通过习得数据来考察，而非通过成人的语法描写。全章的核心理念是：只要身边有可供观察的语言使用者，儿童的心智就有能力极其迅速地习得语法。"},{"en":"By the end, readers should identify the milestones of typical language development and interpret evidence from a range of experimental methods to draw conclusions about children's mental grammar. The chapter also shows how development in a signed language parallels development in a spoken language whenever the child's environment makes that language accessible.","zh":"学完本章，读者应能辨认典型语言发展的各个里程碑，并解读来自多种实验方法的证据，据此推断儿童心理语法的状况。本章还说明，只要环境让儿童能够接触到某一种手语，该手语的发展就与口语的发展相互平行。"},{"en":"A final theme concerns multilingualism: the chapter discusses some of the benefits of acquiring more than one language. Together the milestones, experiments and signed-language evidence point to how much grammar a young mind can build in a very short time.","zh":"最后一个主题涉及多语现象：本章讨论习得一种以上语言所带来的若干益处。里程碑、实验证据与手语证据合在一起，说明幼小的心智能在极短时间内建立起多少语法知识。"}]},"chapter-128-slug-11-1-tiny-powerful-language-learners":{"title":{"en":"11.1 Tiny, powerful language learners","zh":"11.1 幼小却强大的语言学习者"},"summary":{"en":"Newborns can do little beyond sleeping, eating and crying, yet by school age they hold sophisticated conversations without explicit teaching. Their rapid progress comes from brain activity that tracks the ambient language. Deaf children show how vital that input is: language deprivation, driven by oralism, harms development, while early access to ASL supports typical vocabulary growth.","zh":"新生儿除了睡眠、进食和哭泣几乎什么都不会，但到入学年龄已能进行相当复杂的对话，而且并未受过正式教学。这种迅猛进步来自追踪环境语言的大脑活动。聋童的案例显示了这种输入何其关键：由口语法主义驱动的语言剥夺会损害发展，而及早接触美国手语则能支持正常的词汇增长。"},"points":[{"en":"Newborns can only sleep, eat, cry and eliminate, but soon manage complex sentences.","zh":"新生儿只会睡眠、进食、哭泣与排泄，但不久便能说出复杂句子。"},{"en":"Every typically-developing child with access to language becomes fluent, mostly without explicit teaching.","zh":"每个接触得到语言的正常发展儿童都会变得流利，且大多无需明确教学。"},{"en":"The baby brain tracks the ambient language and builds the child's mental grammar from it.","zh":"婴儿大脑追踪环境语言，并据此建立儿童自己的心理语法。"},{"en":"About 90-95% of deaf or hard-of-hearing babies are born to families whose primary modality is speech.","zh":"约 90–95% 的聋儿或听障婴儿出生在主要使用口语的家庭中。"},{"en":"Cochlear implants provide electrical signals that are not a sufficient language environment.","zh":"人工耳蜗提供的是电信号，并不构成充分的语言环境。"},{"en":"Deaf children with ASL by six months develop vocabulary at a rate comparable to signing peers.","zh":"六个月前接触美国手语的聋童，词汇发展速度与聋人父母所生的聋童相当。"}],"terms":[{"en":"ambient language","zh":"环境语言","defEn":"The language used around a child by family, caregivers and older children.","defZh":"儿童周围由家人、照料者与年长儿童所使用的语言。"},{"en":"cochlear implant (CI)","zh":"人工耳蜗","defEn":"A surgically implanted electronic prosthetic that converts sounds into electrical signals.","defZh":"通过手术植入的电子假体装置，把声音转换为电信号。"},{"en":"oralism","zh":"口语法主义（口语至上）","defEn":"The belief that vocal language is better than sign language.","defZh":"认为有声语言优于手语的信念。"},{"en":"language deprivation","zh":"语言剥夺","defEn":"Lack of accessible language input, causing long-term social and cognitive impairments.","defZh":"缺乏可及的语言输入，导致长期的社会与认知功能损害。"},{"en":"modality","zh":"模态","defEn":"The channel a language uses, either auditory-vocal or visual-gestural.","defZh":"语言所使用的通道，即听觉—发音通道或视觉—手势通道。"}],"examples":[{"text":"Mummy, do you remember that time we made chocolate pudding? Maybe we could make some on Saturday. This Saturday, in the afternoon. I don’t need to take a nap. Let’s do it together, and maybe then we can eat some!","noteEn":"An utterance produced by the author's twin at about four and a half years old.","noteZh":"作者的双胞胎孩子约四岁半时说出的语句。"},{"text":"a child aged 1;6 is one year and six months old, or one-and-a-half","noteEn":"The notation convention for writing young children's ages in years and months.","noteZh":"书写幼儿年龄时用分号隔开年与月的记法约定。"}],"body":[{"en":"A newborn can do little but sleep, eat liquid food, eliminate and cry, and cannot focus its eyes or control its limbs. Yet by the time children start school at four or five, most run and jump, some ride bikes, and they hold sophisticated conversations with complex sentences. One of the author's twins, at four and a half, bargained about making chocolate pudding on Saturday afternoon. Every typically-developing child with language access becomes fluent, mostly without explicit teaching.","zh":"新生儿除了睡眠、吃流质食物、排泄和哭泣之外做不了什么，甚至无法聚焦视线或控制四肢。然而到四五岁开始上学时，多数孩子已能奔跑跳跃，有些还会骑车，并能用复杂句子进行有相当难度的对话。作者的一个双胞胎孩子四岁半时，商量星期六下午做巧克力布丁。每个接触得到语言的正常发展儿童都会变得流利，而且大多没有明确教学。"},{"en":"That development comes from immense brain activity responding to the ambient language: the language used by family members, caregivers and older children the child spends time with. The baby brain tracks patterns there and builds the child's mental grammar. English yields a grammar for English, Tamil and Mandarin likewise. If the ambient language is American Sign Language (ASL), the child develops a grammar for ASL, and a two-language environment yields grammars for both.","zh":"这种发展源自大脑针对环境语言的大量活动。环境语言指儿童身边的家人、照料者和年长儿童所使用的语言。婴儿大脑追踪其中的模式，并据此建立儿童自己的心理语法。英语环境产生英语语法，泰米尔语和普通话等环境亦然。若环境语言是美国手语（ASL），儿童就会发展出美国手语的心理语法；双语环境则产生两种语法。"},{"en":"Some children lack any language environment: about 90-95% of babies born deaf or hard of hearing have families whose primary modality is speech. A cochlear implant, surgically implanted, converts sounds into electrical signals sent to the brain via the auditory nerve, and is commonly given between ages one and three. Even so, children with CIs score far below hearing peers on language tests, since those signals are not a sufficient language environment.","zh":"有些儿童接触不到任何语言环境：出生时耳聋或听障的婴儿中，约 90–95% 的家庭主要使用口语模态。人工耳蜗经手术植入，把声音转换为电信号并经听神经传至大脑，通常在一至三岁间植入。即便如此，植入人工耳蜗的儿童在语言测试中仍远低于听力正常的同龄人，因为这些信号并不构成充分的语言环境。"},{"en":"Stigma persists around sign languages, and many parents and professionals consider passing in a hearing world so important that they withhold signed language, fearing it will interfere with spoken language. This belief that vocal language is better than sign language is oralism. Many deaf children meet no language before a CI and afterwards have only the device's atypical signals; such deprivation causes lasting social and cognitive impairments. By contrast, deaf children of hearing parents who access ASL by six months show vocabulary growth comparable to those of deaf signing parents, since grammar's neural connections form only in response to input.","zh":"围绕手语与耳聋的污名依然存在，许多家长和专业人员认为在听人世界中“过关”极其重要，因而拒绝提供手语，担心它干扰口语习得。这种认为有声语言优于手语的信念称为口语法主义。于是许多聋童植入人工耳蜗前接触不到语言，之后也只有装置的非典型信号，这种剥夺造成持久的社会与认知损害。相反，听人父母的聋童若在六个月前接触美国手语，词汇发展与聋人父母的聋童相当，因为语法的神经连接只能在对输入的回应中形成。"}]},"chapter-129-slug-11-2-when-does-language-learning-start":{"title":{"en":"11.2 When does language learning start?","zh":"11.2 语言学习从何时开始？"},"summary":{"en":"For hearing babies, language learning begins before birth. Fetal heart rate rises in response to external sounds at about seven months of pregnancy, and by eight months a fetus responds more to its pregnant parent's voice than to a stranger's. Using high-amplitude sucking, researchers found newborns discriminate French from Russian, and Thai-English babies notice a language switch.","zh":"对听力正常的婴儿来说，语言学习在出生前就已开始。怀孕约七个月时，胎儿心率会因外界声音而升高；到八个月时，胎儿对怀孕父母声音的反应强于对陌生人的反应。研究者用高振幅吮吸法发现，新生儿能区分法语与俄语，泰语—英语双语家庭的婴儿也能察觉语言切换。"},"points":[{"en":"Fetal heart rate increases in response to external sounds at about seven months of pregnancy.","zh":"怀孕约七个月时，胎儿心率会因外界声音而升高。"},{"en":"By eight months, a fetus responds more to its pregnant parent's voice than a stranger's.","zh":"到八个月时，胎儿对怀孕父母声音的反应强于对陌生人声音的反应。"},{"en":"High-amplitude sucking measures interest: babies suck harder, then habituate and recover for new sounds.","zh":"高振幅吮吸法测量兴趣：婴儿吮吸更强，随后习惯化，遇到新声音又恢复。"},{"en":"Newborns of French-speaking parents distinguish French from Russian sentences by the same speaker.","zh":"父母说法语的新生儿能区分同一说话人说的法语与俄语句子。"},{"en":"Newborns of Thai-English bilingual parents notice a switch between English and Thai.","zh":"泰语—英语双语父母的新生儿能察觉英语与泰语之间的切换。"},{"en":"Acquisition is not a race; earlier learning is not necessarily an advantage.","zh":"习得不是竞赛；更早学会未必是优势。"}],"terms":[{"en":"fetus","zh":"胎儿","defEn":"An unborn baby still inside the uterus.","defZh":"尚在子宫内的未出生婴儿。"},{"en":"pressure transducer","zh":"压力传感器","defEn":"An instrument connected to a pacifier that measures how powerfully a baby sucks.","defZh":"连接安抚奶嘴、用于测量婴儿吮吸力度的仪器。"},{"en":"high-amplitude sucking","zh":"高振幅吮吸（法）","defEn":"A habituation method using sucking strength to test what babies notice.","defZh":"以吮吸力度为指标、通过习惯化考察婴儿能否察觉差异的实验方法。"},{"en":"habituation","zh":"习惯化","defEn":"The decrease in response that follows repeated presentation of the same stimulus.","defZh":"同一刺激反复呈现后反应减弱的现象。"},{"en":"prosody","zh":"韵律","defEn":"The rhythmic and melodic pattern of speech, including syllable timing and stress.","defZh":"话语的节奏与旋律模式，包括音节时长与重音。"}],"examples":[{"text":"newborns whose parents speak French notice the difference between French and Russian sentences spoken by the same person","noteEn":"Evidence from the high-amplitude sucking habituation method.","noteZh":"来自高振幅吮吸习惯化方法的证据。"},{"text":"babies born to Thai-English bilingual parents noticed when the spoken language switched from English to Thai","noteEn":"A high-amplitude sucking study conducted in British Columbia.","noteZh":"在不列颠哥伦比亚进行的一项高振幅吮吸研究。"}],"body":[{"en":"Early exposure matters because the mind begins building a mental grammar very young, and for hearing babies that work can start before birth. A fetus's heart rate rises in response to external sounds at about the seven-month point in pregnancy, so it can hear noises from outside. Fetuses retain something of what they hear: by eight months the heart rate rises more for the pregnant parent's voice than for a stranger's, meaning some memory of that voice is stored. After birth heart rate is less informative, since the world offers many other interesting stimuli and newborns cannot report what they know.","zh":"及早接触语言之所以重要，是因为心智在很小的年纪就开始构建心理语法，而对听力正常的婴儿来说，这项工作在出生前就能启动。怀孕约七个月时，胎儿心率会因外界声音而升高，可见胎儿能听到体外的声响。胎儿还会保留所听内容的一部分：到八个月时，心率对怀孕父母声音的升高幅度大于对陌生人声音的反应，说明关于该声音的记忆已经存储下来。出生之后心率提供的信息变少，因为世界中有许多其他有趣的刺激，而新生儿又无法说出自己知道什么。"},{"en":"The high-amplitude sucking habituation method solves that problem. A pressure transducer connected to a pacifier measures how powerfully a baby sucks. A baby interested in a sound sucks harder; if the sound keeps playing, she becomes bored and her sucking strength decreases, which we call habituation. A new sound revives her interest and sucking becomes powerful again. Observing whether sucking strength increases when one sound replaces another therefore reveals whether a baby notices the difference.","zh":"高振幅吮吸习惯化方法解决了这一难题。与安抚奶嘴相连的压力传感器可以测量婴儿吮吸的力度。婴儿对某个声音感兴趣时吮吸更有力；若同一声音持续播放，她会厌倦，吮吸力度下降，这称为习惯化。新声音会重新唤起兴趣，吮吸又变得有力。因此观察声音替换时吮吸力度是否上升，就能知道婴儿是否察觉了差异。"},{"en":"Much of the sound reaching a fetus is muffled, but prosody remains accessible. French rhythm rests on syllables of similar length, whereas Russian rhythm depends on syllable stress; because that prosodic rhythm is audible in the uterus, newborns can separate a familiar rhythm from an unfamiliar one. Newborns of French-speaking parents distinguish French from Russian sentences by the same speaker, and babies of Thai-English bilingual parents in a high-amplitude sucking study in British Columbia noticed a switch from English to Thai, suggesting two mental grammars are already taking shape. Acquisition is not a race, though: children vary hugely, earlier learning is not necessarily an advantage, and there is no evidence that a fetus without in-utero speech, whether deaf or with a signing parent, is disadvantaged.","zh":"传到胎儿耳中的声音大多很模糊，但韵律仍然可及。法语的节奏依赖长度相近的音节，而俄语的节奏依赖音节重音；由于这种韵律节奏在子宫内可以听到，新生儿能把熟悉的节奏与陌生的节奏分开。父母说法语的新生儿能区分同一说话人说出的法语与俄语句子；在不列颠哥伦比亚的一项高振幅吮吸研究中，泰语—英语双语家庭的婴儿察觉到所说语言从英语切换到泰语，说明两种心理语法已在形成。但习得不是竞赛：儿童个体差异极大，更早学会未必是优势，也没有证据表明因胎儿耳聋或父母使用手语而未在子宫内接触语音的胎儿处于不利地位。"}]},"chapter-130-slug-11-3-phonemic-contrast":{"title":{"en":"11.3 Phonemic contrast","zh":"11.3 音位对立"},"summary":{"en":"Hearing babies start building the phonology of their language long before they speak. Using habituation and conditioned head turns, Werker and colleagues showed that six-month-olds notice place-of-articulation contrasts from English, Hindi and Nłeʔkepmxcín alike, but that this sensitivity narrows to about 10-20% for non-native contrasts by age one. Deaf and hearing babies acquiring a sign language follow the same timetable.","zh":"听力正常的婴儿在开口说话之前就已开始构建母语音系。Werker 等人借助习惯化与条件化转头法发现，六个月大的婴儿既能分辨英语的发音部位对立，也能分辨印地语和 Nłeʔkepmxcín 的对立；但到一岁时，他们对非母语对立的敏感度已降至约 10–20%。学习手语的聋婴与健听婴儿表现出相同的时间表。"},"points":[{"en":"Every language organizes the same phonetic differences differently: [pʰ] and [p] are allophones in English, but separate phonemes in Thai.","zh":"语音差异本身各语言相同，但组织方式各异：英语中 [pʰ] 与 [p] 是同一音位的变体，在泰语中却是两个不同音位。"},{"en":"Conditioned head-turn testing infers discrimination when a habituated baby looks back at the speaker after a sound change.","zh":"条件化转头法以婴儿在声音改变后重新转向声源为依据，推断其察觉到了差异。"},{"en":"Six-month-old English-learning babies succeeded on English, Hindi and Nłeʔkepmxcín contrasts at 80-90%, matching no language in particular.","zh":"六个月大的英语婴儿对英语、印地语、Nłeʔkepmxcín 三组对立的成功率均为 80–90%，尚未偏向任何语言。"},{"en":"By ten months success fell to 50-60%, and by one year only 10-20% for the two non-English contrasts.","zh":"到十个月大时成功率降至 50–60%，一岁时对两组非英语对立的成功率仅剩 10–20%。"},{"en":"Researchers found the same perceptual narrowing for ASL handshapes; ASL-exposed babies kept the sensitivity, English-learning babies without ASL lost it.","zh":"研究者在美国手语手形上也发现同样的知觉窄化：接触手语的婴儿保留了敏感性，未接触手语的英语婴儿则失去该能力。"},{"en":"Losing sensitivity does not make new contrasts unlearnable; later learning is simply shaped by the categories built in the first year.","zh":"敏感度下降并不意味着新对立无法习得，只是后续学习会受到第一年所建立范畴的塑造。"}],"terms":[{"en":"phoneme","zh":"音位","defEn":"A contrastive speech unit in a language's mental grammar; replacing it changes meaning.","defZh":"某一语言心理语法中具有对立作用的语音单位，替换它会改变词义。"},{"en":"allophone","zh":"音位变体","defEn":"A predictable phonetic variant of a single phoneme, as [pʰ] and [p] are in English.","defZh":"同一音位在不同语音环境中的可预测变体，如英语中送气的 [pʰ] 与不送气的 [p]。"},{"en":"conditioned head turn","zh":"条件化转头法","defEn":"A habituation procedure that measures whether a baby turns back toward a speaker after a sound change.","defZh":"一种习惯化实验程序，通过观察婴儿在声音改变后是否重新转向声源来判断其辨别能力。"},{"en":"perceptual narrowing","zh":"知觉窄化","defEn":"The first-year decline in sensitivity to phonetic contrasts absent from the language environment.","defZh":"婴儿在第一年内对语言环境中不存在的语音对立逐渐失去敏感度的现象。"},{"en":"place of articulation","zh":"发音部位","defEn":"The location in the vocal tract where a consonant's obstruction is made.","defZh":"辅音发音时声道中形成阻碍的位置，如齿、齿龈、卷舌、软腭或小舌。"}],"examples":[{"text":"[pʰ]","noteEn":"The aspirated stop that is an allophone of English /p/ but a separate phoneme in Thai.","noteZh":"送气塞音，在英语中是 /p/ 的音位变体，在泰语中却是独立的音位。"},{"text":"cat and bat","noteEn":"A familiar English minimal pair illustrating the /k/ versus /b/ phoneme contrast.","noteZh":"熟悉的英语最小对立对，用来说明 /k/ 与 /b/ 的音位对立。"},{"text":"the Hindi contrast between a retroflex stop /ʈa/ and a dental stop /t̪a/","noteEn":"One of the three syllable pairs tested in Werker and Tees's cross-language study.","noteZh":"Werker 与 Tees 跨语言研究中所测三组音节对之一，差别在发音部位。"},{"text":"a Nłeʔkepmxcín contrast between glottalized velar /kʼi/ and uvular /qʼi/ stops","noteEn":"A Salish contrast that English-learning babies could still detect at six months.","noteZh":"一种萨利什语的对立，英语婴儿在六个月大时仍能察觉其差别。"}],"body":[{"en":"The phonology of a language is language-specific: which segments and features contrast and which are merely allophones differs from one language to the next. English treats aspirated [pʰ] and unaspirated [p] as variants of one phoneme, whereas Thai treats them as two. Nobody ever teaches a child that [k] and [b] distinguish cat from bat, so where does that unconscious knowledge come from?","zh":"每种语言的音系都自成系统：哪些音段和特征构成对立、哪些只是音位变体，在不同语言中并不相同。英语把送气的 [pʰ] 与不送气的 [p] 视为同一音位的变体，泰语则视之为两个音位。从没有人教过孩子 [k] 与 [b] 能区分 cat 和 bat，这种无意识的知识从何而来？研究者需要借助实验来回答这个问题。"},{"en":"One method for finding out is the conditioned head-turn procedure. A sound plays from a speaker and the baby turns toward it; after habituating, the baby looks away. If the next sound is the same, the baby stays bored, but a genuinely different sound brings the head back around. Researchers read that head turn as evidence that the baby detected a difference.","zh":"条件化转头法正是探究这一问题的实验手段。扬声器播放声音时婴儿会转向声源，习惯之后便移开视线；若接下来的声音相同，婴儿保持不注意状态，若声音确有差别，婴儿会重新转头。研究者便把这次转头解读为婴儿察觉到了差异的证据，其逻辑与高振幅吸吮法相同。"},{"en":"Janet Werker's team tested three syllable pairs: the English /ba/ and /da/, the Hindi retroflex /ʈa/ against dental /t̪a/, and the Nłeʔkepmxcín glottalized velar /kʼi/ against uvular /qʼi/. English-speaking adults were flawless on English but poor on the other two. Monolingual English-learning babies, however, succeeded on all three at 80-90% at six months, fell to 50-60% by ten months, and managed only 10-20% on the non-English contrasts at one year, already matching adults.","zh":"Janet Werker 的团队测试了三组音节：英语的 /ba/ 与 /da/、印地语的卷舌塞音 /ʈa/ 与齿塞音 /t̪a/，以及 Nłeʔkepmxcín 的声门化软腭塞音 /kʼi/ 与小舌塞音 /qʼi/。说英语的成人在英语对立上毫无差错，在另外两组上却表现很差。而在单语英语环境中成长的婴儿六个月大时三组都达到 80–90% 的成功率，十个月大降至 50–60%，一岁时对非英语对立的成功率仅 10–20%，已与成人相当。"},{"en":"The signed-language research came later but told the same story: babies under six months noticed contrastive ASL handshapes without any ASL exposure, and by fourteen months only the ASL-acquiring babies still did. So whether the language is spoken or signed, a child's mind has built phoneme categories from the ambient contrasts by about age one.","zh":"手语研究开展得更晚，结论却一致：未接触过美国手语的六个月以下婴儿也能察觉具有音位对立的手形差异，而到十四个月大时，只有正在习得美国手语的婴儿仍保持这一敏感性。可见无论语言是口语还是手语，儿童的心理语法都会在约一岁时依据环境中的对立建立起音位范畴。"}]},"chapter-131-slug-11-4-early-production":{"title":{"en":"11.4 Early language production","zh":"11.4 早期语言产出"},"summary":{"en":"Newborns cannot yet talk because their larynx sits high and their articulatory control is still developing, so early productions are random wiggling and gurgling. Around six months, reduplicated syllable-like babbles appear in speech and, for sign-exposed babies, on the hands. First words arrive later, and their meanings are shaped by the child's own experience of the environment.","zh":"新生儿还不会说话，是因为喉位偏高、发音器官的控制尚未成熟，早期产出只是随意的扭动与咕噜声。约六个月大时，口语中出现重复音节的咿呀声，接触手语的婴儿则在手上发出类似产出。首批词出现得更晚，其意义受儿童自身环境经验的塑造。"},"points":[{"en":"Newborns' larynx starts lowering around six months, and control of fingers and arms precedes control of the jaw, tongue and lips.","zh":"新生儿的喉部约在六个月大时开始下降，对手指和手臂的控制早于对下颌、舌头和嘴唇的控制。"},{"en":"Canonical babbling, from about six months, uses reduplicated consonant-vowel syllables such as [babababa], favouring low [a] and voiced stops.","zh":"约六个月大起出现的典型咿呀声由重复的辅音加元音音节构成，如 [babababa]，多使用低元音 [a] 和浊塞音。"},{"en":"Deaf babies start vocal babbling on the same schedule but gradually produce less of it; sign-exposed babies babble with their hands.","zh":"聋婴开始发声咿呀的时间与健听婴儿相同，但日后逐渐减少；处于手语环境中的婴儿则用手咿呀。"},{"en":"Babbling is not random: it uses repeated syllable patterns and a subset of the segments or handshapes present in the environment.","zh":"咿呀声并非随机：它采用重复的音节模式，并且只使用环境语言中部分音段或手形。"},{"en":"A form counts as a word only when it refers: [baba] reaching for a bottle refers, but sounds for fun do not.","zh":"某一形式是否算词取决于语境：伸手要奶瓶或球时说 [baba] 算词，纯粹为发声取乐则只是咿呀。"},{"en":"Children's meanings may be overextended or underextended, as when apple covers all roundish fruit or elephant names only one stuffed toy.","zh":"儿童词义可能过度扩展或扩展不足，例如把 apple 用于所有圆形水果，或只用 elephant 指某一个毛绒玩具。"}],"terms":[{"en":"canonical babbling","zh":"典型咿呀声","defEn":"Reduplicated consonant-vowel babble such as [babababa], typical from about six months.","defZh":"自约六个月大起出现的重复性辅音加元音咿呀声，如 [babababa]，是婴儿习得音节结构的最早表现之一。"},{"en":"articulator","zh":"发音器官","defEn":"A movable part of the vocal tract, such as the tongue, lips or jaw, used to produce speech.","defZh":"声道中可以活动的部分，如舌头、嘴唇和下颌，发音时通过改变其位置来形成不同的语音。"},{"en":"proximal articulator","zh":"近端发音器官","defEn":"A sign articulator closer to the torso, such as the elbow or wrist.","defZh":"手语中位置更靠近躯干的发音器官，如肘部和腕部，手语婴儿最早的手部咿呀多用这类器官。"},{"en":"distal articulator","zh":"远端发音器官","defEn":"A sign articulator farther from the torso, such as the fingers or knuckles.","defZh":"手语中位置离躯干较远的发音器官，如手指和指关节，其控制能力比近端器官发育得更晚。"},{"en":"overextension","zh":"过度扩展","defEn":"Applying a word more broadly than adults do, so that apple names many round fruits.","defZh":"把某个词的使用范围扩大到超出成人的程度，如用 apple 指称各种圆形水果。"},{"en":"underextension","zh":"扩展不足","defEn":"Applying a word more narrowly than adults do, so that elephant names only one toy.","defZh":"把某个词的适用范围限制得比成人更窄，如 elephant 只指某一个玩具。"}],"examples":[{"text":"[babababa]","noteEn":"The classic canonical babble, built from repeated low vowels and voiced stops.","noteZh":"最典型的咿呀声，由重复的低元音与浊塞音构成。"},{"text":"[badibadi]","noteEn":"A later babble in which the child varies both consonants and vowels.","noteZh":"后期咿呀声的例子，儿童在其中已能变换辅音和元音，不再只是重复同一音节。"},{"text":"Apple!","noteEn":"A toddler's overextended label for a pumpkin seen for the first time.","noteZh":"幼儿初次见到南瓜时所说的话，属于词义的过度扩展。"},{"text":"look up","noteEn":"The instruction to which blind Kelli responded by raising her hands rather than her head.","noteZh":"研究者给出的指令，盲童 Kelli 听到后举手而非抬头作为回应。"}],"body":[{"en":"Babies learn a great deal about their language before they can talk, and their silence is largely physical. A newborn's larynx sits higher than an adult's and only begins to lower at about six months. Control of the body also comes gradually: fingers, hands and forearms first, then the jaw, tongue and lips. In the first months, hand movements and vocalizations are mostly random wiggling and gurgling.","zh":"婴儿在会说话之前已学到大量语言知识，迟迟不开口的原因主要是生理上的。新生儿的喉位比成人高，约六个月大时才开始下降。身体控制能力也是逐步获得的：先能控制手指、手和手臂，之后才轮到下颌、舌头和嘴唇。出生后最初几个月里，手部动作和发声大多只是随意的扭动与咕噜声。"},{"en":"From about six months the sounds gain syllable structure. Babies produce reduplicated consonant-vowel syllables, typically with the low vowel [a] and voiced stops, because a wide-open and a fully obstructed tract is easier to alternate than partial obstruction, and keeping the vocal folds vibrating avoids voicing switches. Canonical babbling therefore sounds like [babababa] or [dadadada], later becoming more varied, as in [badibadi] or [ɡudaɡuda].","zh":"从约六个月大起，婴儿发出的声音开始具备音节结构。他们会产出重复的辅音加元音音节，多用低元音 [a] 和浊塞音，因为让声道在完全张开与完全阻塞之间交替、并始终保持声带振动，比形成部分阻碍或反复切换清浊要容易。因此典型咿呀声听起来像 [babababa] 或 [dadadada]，此后逐渐变得多样，如 [badibadi] 或 [ɡudaɡuda]。"},{"en":"Vocal babbling begins on the same schedule for hearing and deaf babies, though deaf babies gradually produce less of it. When the ambient language is signed, babies babble on their hands, using handshapes from the environment and favouring proximal articulators like elbows and wrists over distal ones. Either way the babble is structured: repeated syllable-like patterns, alternation between handshape and path movement, and a subset of ambient segments or handshapes.","zh":"健听婴儿与聋婴发声咿呀的时间表相同，只是聋婴日后逐渐减少。当环境语言是手语时，婴儿改用手来咿呀，使用环境中的手形，并更多使用肘、腕等近端发音器官而非手指等远端器官。无论哪种模态，咿呀都有结构：重复的音节式模式，手形与路径运动之间或闭合与开放声道之间的交替，以及只取用环境中部分音段或手形。"},{"en":"Distinguishing babbling from first words requires the context, because a word links a form to a meaning. An English-acquiring child who says [baba] while reaching for a bottle or a ball is referring and therefore producing a word, even though the adult forms are [bɑɾəl] and [bɑl]; the same form produced purely for fun is non-referential babble. Sign-acquiring babies usually sign their first words around 0;8 or 0;9, earlier than the 1;0 typical of spoken language, perhaps because arm and hand control develops sooner or because signs are more often iconic.","zh":"要区分咿呀与首批词必须依据语境，因为词把形式与意义联系在一起。习得英语的儿童在伸手要奶瓶或球时说 [baba]，是在进行指称，因此算作词，尽管成人形式是 [bɑɾəl] 和 [bɑl]；若只是为发声取乐而发出同一形式，则属于无指称的咿呀。习得手语的婴儿通常在 0;8 或 0;9 左右打出首批词，早于口语常见的 1;0，原因可能是手臂和手部控制发育更早，也可能因为手语词更多具有象似性。"}]},"chapter-132-slug-11-5-the-language-environment-and-the-so-called-word-gap":{"title":{"en":"11.5 The Language environment and the so-called word gap","zh":"11.5 语言环境与所谓的词汇缺口"},"summary":{"en":"Hart and Risley's 1995 study produced the famous claim that poor children hear thirty million fewer words by age three, a phrase that has shaped policy but also stigmatized low-income parents. A 2018 follow-up that counted all speech in the environment, not just mothers' speech to the child, found no clear socioeconomic pattern and even an advantage in some poor Black communities. The case shows how measurement choices can bias supposedly objective findings.","zh":"Hart 与 Risley 1995 年的研究提出了著名论断：贫困家庭的儿童到三岁时少听到三千万个词，这一说法影响了政策，也给低收入家长带来污名。2018 年的后续研究改以环境中全部言语为计数对象，而非只计母亲对孩子说的话，结果未发现明确的社会经济模式，部分贫困黑人社区甚至更具优势。此案例显示测量选择本身就可能使所谓客观的结论产生偏差。"},"points":[{"en":"The language environment matters: hearing babies learn speech patterns before birth, and deaf babies learn sign patterns once exposed to them.","zh":"语言环境至关重要：健听婴儿在出生前就开始学习语音模式，聋婴一旦接触手语便开始学习其模式。"},{"en":"Hart and Risley reported that three-year-olds in poor families heard thirty million fewer words than affluent peers, the '30 million word gap'.","zh":"Hart 与 Risley 报告称，贫困家庭的儿童三岁时比富裕家庭的同龄人少听到三千万个词，由此产生「三千万词汇缺口」之说。"},{"en":"The 1995 count included only words the mother spoke directly to the child, a measure favouring white middle-class stay-at-home mothers.","zh":"1995 年的统计只计入母亲直接对孩子说的话，这一测量方式偏向白人中产阶层全职母亲与儿童的互动模式。"},{"en":"The affluent families studied were largely white and the poor families almost entirely Black, so cultural differences in interaction went unaccounted for.","zh":"所研究的富裕家庭大多是白人，贫困家庭几乎全是黑人，因此成人与儿童互动方式上的文化差异未被纳入考虑。"},{"en":"Counting all caregivers and ambient language, Sperry found the word gap gone and poor Black households with the most words.","zh":"在统计所有照护者以及环境中全部言语后，Sperry 等人发现词汇缺口消失，贫困黑人家庭每小时听到的词数反而最多。"},{"en":"A 2021 meta-analysis concluded that socioeconomic status is not a good predictor of the quality of a child's language environment.","zh":"2021 年的一项元分析得出结论：社会经济地位并不能很好地预测儿童语言环境的质量。"}],"terms":[{"en":"language environment","zh":"语言环境","defEn":"The speech or sign input available to a learner, including what is overheard rather than addressed to them.","defZh":"学习者所能接触到的口语或手语输入，包括并非对其直接说出的旁听言语。"},{"en":"word gap","zh":"词汇缺口","defEn":"The claimed difference in the number of words poor and affluent children hear by age three.","defZh":"所谓贫困家庭与富裕家庭儿童在三岁前所听到词数上的差距。"},{"en":"socioeconomic status","zh":"社会经济地位","defEn":"A measure combining income, education and occupation, often used to compare family environments.","defZh":"综合收入、教育与职业的衡量指标，研究家庭环境时常用它来划分不同的社会群体。"},{"en":"meta-analysis","zh":"元分析","defEn":"A study that statistically combines the results of many separate studies on one question.","defZh":"把针对同一问题的多项独立研究结果在统计上加以合并的研究方法。"},{"en":"primary caregiver","zh":"主要照护者","defEn":"The person who provides most of a child's day-to-day care and interaction.","defZh":"承担儿童日常照料与互动主要责任的人，通常是父母之一，1995 年的统计只计算了这个人对孩子说的话。"}],"examples":[{"text":"thirty million fewer words","noteEn":"The most quoted figure from Hart and Risley, which became the '30 million word gap'.","noteZh":"Hart 与 Risley 研究中最常被引用的数字，后来被概括为「三千万词汇缺口」。"}],"body":[{"en":"Environment clearly matters for young learners. Hearing babies begin absorbing speech patterns before birth, and deaf babies begin absorbing sign patterns as soon as those patterns are available to them. Most obviously, which language a child acquires depends on which language surrounds them, which naturally raises the question of whether differences in that environment affect children acquiring the same language.","zh":"环境对幼儿学习者的重要性显而易见。健听婴儿在出生前就开始吸收语音模式，聋婴一旦能接触到手语模式便立即开始吸收。最直接的一点是，儿童习得哪种语言取决于周围存在哪种语言，这自然引出新的问题：对习得同一种语言的儿童而言，环境差异是否会影响其语言发展。"},{"en":"Hart and Risley's influential 1995 comparison of American children from different socioeconomic and racial groups reported what they called staggering contrasts between rich and poor families. Their most quoted claim is that by age three, children in poor families had heard thirty million fewer words than children in middle-class and affluent families. The catchy phrase '30 million word gap' spread widely and prompted policy decisions and early-childhood interventions, but it also stigmatized low-income parents.","zh":"Hart 与 Risley 在 1995 年比较了不同社会经济与种族背景的美国儿童，报告称富裕家庭与贫困家庭之间存在「惊人的反差」。其中最常被引用的主张是：贫困家庭的儿童到三岁时比中产及富裕家庭的儿童少听到三千万个词。朗朗上口的「三千万词汇缺口」说法广为流传，推动了政策决策与幼儿教育干预，但同时也给低收入家长带来污名，仿佛在指责他们不常与孩子说话。"},{"en":"The 1995 analysis counted only words the mother spoke directly to the child. It excluded speech addressed to the child by anyone else and speech from nearby conversations not directed at the child, so the measure favoured the interaction style of white, middle-class, stay-at-home mothers. Its other flaw was demographic: the affluent families studied were largely white and the poor families almost entirely Black, so cultural and linguistic differences in how adults interact with children went unaccounted for.","zh":"1995 年的分析只统计母亲直接对孩子说的话，未计入其他人对孩子说的话，也未计入旁边并非针对孩子的对话，因此这一测量偏向白人中产阶层全职母亲与儿童的互动方式。其另一处缺陷是人口构成：所研究的富裕家庭大多是白人，贫困家庭几乎全是黑人，于是成人与儿童互动方式上的文化和语言差异未被纳入考虑。"},{"en":"The 2018 follow-up argued that children also learn from overheard language, so it added further measures. With the 1995 measure there was no clear socioeconomic pattern; counting speech by all caregivers, and then all language in the environment, the households with the most words per hour were poor Black families. The researchers reported that the Word Gap disappeared and that some poor and working-class communities showed an advantage, while variation within each socioeconomic stratum was large. A 2021 meta-analysis likewise found socioeconomic status a poor predictor.","zh":"2018 年的后续研究主张，儿童也能从旁听到的语言中学习，因此增加了更多测量方式。按 1995 年的方式统计时并未出现明确的社会经济模式；而统计所有照护者对孩子说的话、进而统计环境中全部言语时，每小时词数最多的反而是贫困黑人家庭。研究者报告词汇缺口消失，一些贫困与工薪阶层社区甚至显示优势，同时同一阶层内部的差异极大。2021 年的元分析同样发现社会经济地位难以预测语言环境。"}]},"chapter-133-slug-11-6-understanding-word-combinations":{"title":{"en":"11.6 Understanding word combinations","zh":"11.6 理解词语组合"},"summary":{"en":"Babies understand far more language than they produce, so researchers use preferential looking to probe their knowledge. Split-screen studies show that six- to ten-month-olds link word forms to meanings, and that children as young as fifteen months use word order to choose the matching scene. Toy experiments further reveal that one-year-olds read novel words differently in noun and adjective frames, and two-year-olds are sensitive to verb subcategories.","zh":"婴儿能理解的语言远多于他们能产出的语言，因此研究者借助优先注视法探查其语言知识。分屏实验表明，六到十个月的婴儿已把词形与意义联系起来，十五个月大的孩子还能依据词序选择与句子相符的场景。玩具实验进一步显示，一岁幼儿能区分名词框架与形容词框架中的生造词，两岁儿童对动词次范畴也已敏感。"},"points":[{"en":"Babies' comprehension outruns their production, so researchers must use indirect experimental methods to observe what they understand.","zh":"婴儿的理解能力远超产出能力，研究者必须借助间接实验方法来观察他们究竟理解了什么。"},{"en":"In preferential looking, babies watch a split screen while a recorded voice names one of two objects.","zh":"在优先注视法中，婴儿观看分屏画面，同时录音说出其中一件物体的名称。"},{"en":"Six-month-olds look at the named object above chance, and by ten months the effect is reliable.","zh":"六个月大的婴儿看向被命名物体的比例已高于随机水平，到十个月时这种表现相当稳定。"},{"en":"With two similar scenes, fifteen-month-olds choose the one matching the sentence, showing sensitivity to constituent structure.","zh":"面对两个相似场景时，十五个月大的孩子会选择与句子相符的一个，说明他们对句法成分结构已经敏感。"},{"en":"Novel words in noun frames are taken as category names, while those in adjective frames are taken as properties.","zh":"出现在名词框架中的生造词被理解为类别名称，出现在形容词框架中的则被理解为属性。"},{"en":"Two-year-olds use transitive and intransitive frames to infer whether a novel verb involves two participants or one.","zh":"两岁儿童能依据及物与不及物框架，推断生造动词涉及一个还是两个参与者。"}],"terms":[{"en":"preferential looking","zh":"优先注视法","defEn":"An experimental method that records where infants look in response to spoken language.","defZh":"一种通过记录婴儿听到话语时注视方向来研究语言理解的实验方法。"},{"en":"compositionality","zh":"组合性原则","defEn":"The meaning of a sentence depends both on word meanings and on how words combine.","defZh":"句子的意义不仅由各个词的意义决定，也由这些词的组合方式决定。"},{"en":"syntactic category","zh":"句法范畴","defEn":"A class of words sharing grammatical distribution, such as noun or adjective.","defZh":"根据语法分布划分出来的词类，如名词、动词、形容词等。"},{"en":"transitive frame","zh":"及物框架","defEn":"A sentence pattern in which a verb takes both a subject and an object.","defZh":"一种句法模式，其中动词同时带有主语和宾语两个论元。"},{"en":"intransitive frame","zh":"不及物框架","defEn":"A sentence pattern in which a verb takes a subject but no object.","defZh":"一种句法模式，其中动词只带主语而不带宾语，因而只有一个论元。"},{"en":"novel word","zh":"生造词","defEn":"A made-up word that children have never heard before the experiment.","defZh":"实验者临时编造出来、儿童此前从未听到过的词，用以测试其理解策略。"}],"examples":[{"text":"Look! Can you find the bear?","noteEn":"The recorded sentence in a preferential looking task names one of the two pictures.","noteZh":"优先注视任务中播放的录音句子，用来命名两幅图片中的一幅。"},{"text":"Look! The kid is chasing the woman!","noteEn":"Only one of the two scenes matches this sentence, so word order matters.","noteZh":"两个场景中只有一个与该句相符，因此词序对理解至关重要。"},{"text":"These are blickets. This one is a blicket and this one is a blicket.","noteEn":"A novel word presented in a noun frame, leading children to choose by category.","noteZh":"生造词出现在名词框架中，使儿童按类别而非颜色作出选择。"},{"text":"The lady is mooping my brother. The lady and my brother are mooping.","noteEn":"The transitive and intransitive frames tested whether two-year-olds track verb subcategories.","noteZh":"及物与不及物两种框架用来检验两岁儿童是否掌握动词次范畴。"}],"body":[{"en":"Babies begin learning phonology at birth and lexical semantics before their first birthday. First words appear around twelve months, and word combinations at roughly eighteen to twenty-four months. Yet comprehension far outruns production, and is much harder to observe, so researchers need indirect methods to probe what toddlers know about syntax.","zh":"婴儿从出生起就开始习得音位系统，一岁前已开始掌握词汇语义。他们约十二个月说出第一个词，十八到二十四个月开始组合词语。然而理解远超产出，且更难观察，研究者需借助间接方法了解幼儿已掌握哪些句法知识。"},{"en":"One method is preferential looking. A baby faces a split screen showing two pictures while a recorded voice says something like \"Look! Can you find the bear?\" Researchers record head turns or eye movements. Babies look reliably at the named object by about ten months, and above chance at six months. When the two sides show the same participants in different configurations, the sentence \"Look! The kid is chasing the woman!\" matches only one. Fifteen-month-olds look more often at that scene, suggesting sensitivity to how words are combined.","zh":"一种方法是优先注视法。婴儿面对分成两半的屏幕，两侧各有一幅图片，录音播放类似「Look! Can you find the bear?」的句子，研究者记录其转头方向或眼动。婴儿到十个月左右能稳定看向被命名的物体，六个月时已高于随机水平。当两侧是同一组参与者但配置不同的场景时，「Look! The kid is chasing the woman!」只与其中一个相符，十五个月大的孩子更常看向那个场景，说明他们对词语组合的方式已经敏感。"},{"en":"Experiments with toys. Booth and Waxman (2003) taught 14-month-olds a made-up word, blickets, in a noun frame: \"These are blickets. This one is a blicket and this one is a blicket.\" Asked for \"the blicket\", children reached for a new toy of the same category but a different colour. When the word appeared in an adjective frame, blickish, they chose the toy matching in colour. One-year-olds thus treat a novel word in noun position as naming a thing or category, and one in adjective position as naming a property.","zh":"另一些实验改用玩具。Booth 和 Waxman（2003）用名词框架把生造词 blickets 教给十四个月大的婴儿：「These are blickets. This one is a blicket and this one is a blicket.」要「the blicket」时，婴儿去拿同类别但颜色不同的新玩具；同一个词换成形容词框架 blickish，他们就选择颜色相同的玩具。可见一岁幼儿把名词位置的新词理解为指称事物或类别，把形容词位置的新词理解为属性。"},{"en":"By two, children are sensitive to verb subcategories too. In a split-screen study by Arunachalam and Waxman (2010), the novel verb mooping appeared in a transitive frame, \"The lady is mooping my brother,\" and two-year-olds looked more often at a scene where one participant acts on the other, such as pushing. In the intransitive frame \"The lady and my brother are mooping,\" they looked more often at a scene where both participants do the same activity, such as waving. Children thus know a great deal about word combination before producing it themselves.","zh":"到两岁时，儿童对动词的次范畴也已敏感。在 Arunachalam 和 Waxman（2010）的分屏实验中，生造动词 mooping 出现在及物框架「The lady is mooping my brother」里时，两岁儿童更常看向一个参与者对另一个参与者施加动作（如推）的场景；而出现在不及物框架「The lady and my brother are mooping」里时，他们更常看向两个参与者共同做同一活动（如挥手）的场景。可见在儿童自己把词组合成短语之前很久，他们就已经相当了解词语组合的方式。"}]},"chapter-134-slug-11-7-syntax-in-early-utterances":{"title":{"en":"11.7 Syntax in early utterances","zh":"11.7 早期话语中的句法"},"summary":{"en":"From about 1;6 to 2;0 children begin combining words, but their telegraphic utterances contain mostly content words. Large corpora show almost no violations of syntactic category, and the rare unusual forms reflect productive derivation. Children also ask simple wh-questions with the wh-word moved to the front, and elicitation studies reveal that even complex embedded questions show structure paralleling adult grammar.","zh":"从一岁半到两岁起，儿童开始把词组合起来，但话语多为电报式，主要包含实词。大规模语料显示，儿童的词类误用极少，个别不寻常的形式其实反映了富有生成性的派生过程。儿童还会把 wh 词移到句首提出简单疑问句；诱导实验则表明，即使复杂的嵌入疑问句也已具备与成人语法平行的结构。"},"points":[{"en":"At 1;6 to 2;0 children begin combining two or three words into telegraphic utterances with few function words.","zh":"一岁半到两岁时，儿童开始把两三个词组合成电报式话语，其中功能词很少。"},{"en":"Across over 200 hours of child speech (Cazden 1968; Maratsos 1982), almost no syntactic category errors appeared.","zh":"两百多小时儿童话语语料中（Cazden 1968；Maratsos 1982）几乎无词类误用。"},{"en":"Forms like crackering come from a productive process that also derives the verb to salt from the noun salt.","zh":"crackering 这类形式来自能产派生，正如名词 salt 可派生出动词 to salt。"},{"en":"English-acquiring children ask questions such as Where kitty? and Who crying? soon after they begin combining words.","zh":"习得英语的儿童开始组词后不久就会问 Where kitty? 和 Who crying? 这类问题。"},{"en":"Sign-acquiring children produced wh-questions as young as 1;7 in ASL and Brazilian Sign Language.","zh":"习得手语的儿童最早在一岁七个月就能产出 wh 疑问句，见于美国手语和巴西手语。"},{"en":"Elicitation with puppets shows preschoolers move the wh-word to the front but also pronounce it in its original position.","zh":"用玩偶进行的诱导实验显示，学龄前儿童把 wh 词移到句首，同时又在原位把它读出来。"}],"terms":[{"en":"telegraphic","zh":"电报式的","defEn":"Describing early child utterances that keep content words and omit most function words.","defZh":"形容儿童早期话语只保留实词、省略大多数功能词的特点。"},{"en":"corpus","zh":"语料库","defEn":"A large collection of recorded speech used for linguistic analysis.","defZh":"为语言分析而收集的大量真实话语材料，通常经过转写和标注。"},{"en":"elicitation","zh":"诱导法","defEn":"A method that creates a context encouraging children to produce a particular structure.","defZh":"通过设计具体情境来促使儿童产出某一特定句法结构的方法。"},{"en":"embedded clause","zh":"嵌入小句","defEn":"A clause that appears inside another clause, often as a complement.","defZh":"出现在另一个小句内部、通常充当补足语或修饰语的小句。"},{"en":"wh-question","zh":"wh 疑问句","defEn":"A question containing a wh-word such as who, what or where.","defZh":"包含 who、what、where 等 wh 词的疑问句，通常需要移位。"},{"en":"generativity","zh":"生成性","defEn":"The property of a grammar that lets speakers create and understand novel forms.","defZh":"语法使说话者能够创造并理解前所未有的新形式与新句子的属性。"}],"examples":[{"text":"Mummy trousers me. I'm crackering my soup. I want to comfortable you.","noteEn":"The rare non-adult forms found in the corpus, all showing category flexibility.","noteZh":"语料中发现的少数非成人形式，都体现了词类的灵活运用。"},{"text":"Where kitty? Who crying?","noteEn":"Early child questions with the wh-word at the beginning, as in adult English.","noteZh":"儿童早期疑问句，wh 词像成人英语那样位于句首，其余成分则被省略。"},{"text":"Who do you think ___ will win the election? What did Lexi say she wanted ___ for lunch?","noteEn":"The target embedded wh-questions, whose declarative counterparts show where the wh-word originates.","noteZh":"实验目标的嵌入 wh 疑问句，其陈述句形式显示 wh 词原本的位置。"},{"text":"Who do you think who wants to hug Grover? What do you think what's in that box?","noteEn":"Children's answers moved the wh-word but also kept it in the embedded position.","noteZh":"儿童产出的句子既把 wh 词移到句首，又保留了它在嵌入小句中的原位。"}],"body":[{"en":"Beginning around age 1;6 to 2;0, most children combine words into phrases of two or even three words. These telegraphic utterances contain mostly content words such as nouns and verbs, with few function words and few inflectional morphemes. Whether they carry syntactic structure is hard to tell.","zh":"大约从一岁半到两岁起，多数儿童开始把词组合成两三个词的短语。这些电报式话语大多是名词、动词等实词，功能词和屈折语素很少。它们是否具有句法结构，很难一眼看出。"},{"en":"Large corpus studies (Cazden, 1968; Maratsos, 1982) searched children's speech for words used in violation of their syntactic category, such as a noun used as a verb. Across more than 200 hours of recording, almost no category errors appeared. The few examples, such as \"Mummy trousers me,\" \"I'm crackering my soup,\" and \"I want to comfortable you,\" actually show generativity: English freely derives verbs from nouns, as when salt yields to salt, meaning to sprinkle salt on something. So a child who derives crackering from cracker is using the grammar productively, and syntactic categories look robust even in early utterances.","zh":"针对儿童话语的大规模语料研究（Cazden, 1968；Maratsos, 1982）寻找违反词类的用法，例如把名词当作动词。在两百多小时录音中几乎找不到词类误用。少数例子如「Mummy trousers me.」「I'm crackering my soup.」「I want to comfortable you.」其实体现了生成性：英语常由名词派生出动词，正如 salt 可派生出意为「撒盐」的 to salt。因此，把 cracker 派生出 crackering 的孩子是在能产地运用语法，词类在早期话语中已相当稳固。"},{"en":"Corpus data show that English-acquiring children begin asking questions soon after they start combining words. Simple questions such as \"Where kitty?\" and \"Who crying?\" are common, with the wh-word moved to the front as in adult English, while why questions appear later. Sign-acquiring children produce wh-questions as young as 1;7 in ASL and Brazilian Sign Language (LSB).","zh":"语料数据表明，习得英语的儿童开始组词后不久就会提问。像「Where kitty?」和「Who crying?」这样的简单疑问句很常见，wh 词与成人英语一样移到句首；why 疑问句出现得稍晚。习得手语的儿童最早在一岁七个月就能产出 wh 疑问句，见于美国手语（ASL）和巴西手语（LSB）。"},{"en":"Complex structures are rare in speech, so researchers use elicitation, often with puppets. Rosalind Thornton studied embedded wh-questions with a blindfolded bear puppet: the child hid toys in boxes, then asked the bear to guess what was inside. Crain and Thornton (1991) asked whether children's grammars allow a wh-word to originate inside an embedded clause, as in \"Who do you think ___ will win the election?\" and \"What did Lexi say she wanted ___ for lunch?\" Some children asked \"Who do you think who wants to hug Grover?\" or \"What do you think what's in that box?\" They moved the wh-word to the front like adults but also pronounced it in its original position.","zh":"复杂结构在自然话语中很少出现，因此研究者采用诱导法，常借助玩偶。Rosalind Thornton 用一只蒙眼的小熊玩偶研究嵌入 wh 疑问句：先让孩子把玩具藏进盒子，再请孩子问小熊猜猜里面是什么。Crain 和 Thornton（1991）想弄清儿童的语法是否允许 wh 词来自嵌入小句内部，如「Who do you think ___ will win the election?」和「What did Lexi say she wanted ___ for lunch?」。有孩子问出「Who do you think who wants to hug Grover?」或「What do you think what's in that box?」。他们像成人一样把 wh 词移到句首，同时又在原位把它读了出来。"}]},"chapter-135-slug-11-8-developing-meaning":{"title":{"en":"11.8. Developing word meanings","zh":"11.8 词义的发展"},"summary":{"en":"Children's semantic knowledge develops in parallel with their syntax. English-acquiring children respect the mass/count distinction early, and four-year-olds interpret more string and more strings differently. Mandarin-acquiring children use classifiers to make the same distinction. Experiments with puppets show that even preschoolers interpret gradable adjectives relative to context and apply predicates like round to individual items.","zh":"儿童的语义知识与其句法能力同步发展。习得英语的儿童很早就遵守可数与不可数的区分，四岁儿童对 more string 与 more strings 的理解明显不同；习得汉语普通话的儿童则用量词表达同样的区分。玩偶实验显示，学龄前儿童已能依据语境理解程度形容词，并把 round 这类谓语用于个体事物。"},"points":[{"en":"Singular count nouns require a determiner in English, while mass nouns take no determiner and resist plurals.","zh":"英语中单数可数名词必须带限定词，不可数名词则不带限定词，也不能有复数形式。"},{"en":"Before age 2;0 children rarely pluralized mass nouns, though plurals like dogs and balls were common.","zh":"两岁前儿童很少把不可数名词变成复数，尽管 dogs、balls 这类复数形式已经很常见。"},{"en":"Four-year-olds chose several small strings for more strings and the single pile for more string.","zh":"四岁儿童听到 more strings 时选几段短线，听到 more string 时选那一整团。"},{"en":"Mandarin marks the mass/count distinction with classifiers; three-year-olds chose the matching object about 60% of the time.","zh":"汉语普通话用量词标记可数与不可数的区分，三岁儿童选择相符物体的正确率约六成。"},{"en":"Children treated big as context-dependent, choosing the bigger block even when both blocks were big.","zh":"儿童把 big 理解为依赖语境的，即使两块积木都大，也选择相对更大的那一块。"},{"en":"Children over three pointed to round buttons rather than triangular buttons arranged in a circle.","zh":"三岁以上的儿童会指向圆形纽扣，而不是摆成圆形的三角形纽扣。"}],"terms":[{"en":"count noun","zh":"可数名词","defEn":"A noun that can be pluralized and needs a determiner in the singular in English.","defZh":"在英语中可以构成复数、且单数形式通常需要限定词的名词。"},{"en":"mass noun","zh":"不可数名词","defEn":"A noun that resists pluralization and appears without a determiner in English.","defZh":"在英语中一般不能构成复数、也不带限定词的名词，如 rice。"},{"en":"classifier","zh":"量词","defEn":"A function word that marks the semantic category of a noun, as in Mandarin.","defZh":"标记名词语义类别的功能词，汉语普通话用量词区分可数与不可数。"},{"en":"gradable adjective","zh":"程度形容词","defEn":"An adjective whose meaning involves a degree on a context-dependent scale.","defZh":"意义涉及某一程度、并依赖语境确定量级的形容词，如 tall。"},{"en":"non-gradable adjective","zh":"非程度形容词","defEn":"An adjective that does not denote a degree and resists comparison or very.","defZh":"不表示程度、也不能受 very 修饰或构成比较级的形容词，如 wooden。"}],"examples":[{"text":"I want a cookie. *I want cookie. I want cookies. *I want a rice. I want rice. *I want rices. I want three cookies. *I want three rices.","noteEn":"The morphosyntactic contrasts between count and mass nouns in English.","noteZh":"英语中可数名词与不可数名词在形态句法上的系统对比，星号表示不合语法。"},{"text":"Who has more strings? Who has more string?","noteEn":"The two questions that elicited different choices in the string experiment.","noteZh":"线绳实验中引出了不同选择结果的两个问题。"},{"text":"Mǐqí shuō tā yào ___ something. Gàosù lǎoshī mǐqí yào ___ shénme.","noteEn":"The Mandarin frame whose blank held either a count-classifier or a mass-classifier.","noteZh":"普通话测试句，空白处由实验者填入可数量词或不可数量词。"},{"text":"But I have TWO red ones! Point to the round buttons.","noteEn":"Children's objection to an ambiguous request, and the button test instruction.","noteZh":"儿童对有歧义请求的异议，以及纽扣测试中玩偶给出的指令。"}],"body":[{"en":"English distinguishes count nouns like pencils and cookies from mass nouns like rice and money: singular count nouns need a determiner (I want a cookie), while mass nouns need none but resist plurals. Gordon (1988) studied two English-acquiring children between 1;9 and 3;6; before 2;0 they rarely pluralized mass nouns, though plurals like dogs and balls were common. Barner and Snedeker (2005) showed four-year-olds string pictures: \"Who has more strings?\" drew the several short pieces, \"Who has more string?\" the single pile.","zh":"英语把 pencils、cookies 这样的可数名词与 rice、money 这样的不可数名词区分开来：单数可数名词必须带限定词（I want a cookie），不可数名词不带限定词，却也不能有复数。Gordon（1988）研究了两名习得英语的儿童（一岁九个月到三岁六个月）：两岁前他们很少把不可数名词变成复数，而 dogs、balls 这类复数形式已很常见。Barner 和 Snedeker（2005）给四岁儿童看线绳图片，听到「Who has more strings?」时他们选择几段短线，听到「Who has more string?」时选择那一整团。"},{"en":"Mandarin encodes this difference with classifiers, function words marking the semantic category of nouns. Chien et al. (2003) had children help a Mickey Mouse toy learning Chinese. Each trial offered three choices, two individual objects and one substance like rice, after a sentence containing a count- or mass-classifier and ending in an unknown word. Guessing gives about 33% correct, but three-year-olds reached about 60%, and six-year-olds were adult-like.","zh":"汉语普通话用量词而非形态手段编码这一差别，量词是标记名词语义类别的功能词。Chien 等（2003）让孩子帮助一个正在学说汉语的米老鼠玩偶：每次测试有三个选项，两件个体物体和一种物质（如米），句中含可数量词或不可数量词，句末则是他们不认识的词。纯靠猜约有 33% 正确，而三岁儿童已达约 60%，六岁儿童则达到成人水平。"},{"en":"Gradable adjectives such as tall describe a degree on a context-dependent scale, whereas non-gradable adjectives such as wooden do not. Syrett et al. (2010) asked three- to five-year-olds to help a puppet ask for things. Faced with a red circle and a red square, children did not simply pick one red item; they objected with \"But I have TWO red ones!\" Asked for \"the big one\" among blocks that differed in size, they chose the bigger block even when both were big.","zh":"tall 这类程度形容词表示依赖语境的量级上的程度，wooden 这样的非程度形容词则不然。Syrett 等（2010）请三到五岁儿童帮玩偶要东西。面对一个红圆圈和一个红方块，孩子不会随便挑一个红色的，而是提出异议：「But I have TWO red ones!」。当玩偶在大小有别的积木中要「the big one」时，即使两块都大，他们也选择相对更大的那块。"},{"en":"Syrett (2015) used button pictures to test predicates. Children saw buttons of various sizes, colours and shapes, then star-shaped buttons arranged into the outline of a star. At test, triangle-shaped buttons arranged into a circle appeared beside circle-shaped buttons arranged into a triangle, and the puppet said, \"Point to the round buttons.\" Children over three reliably chose the round buttons, and even two-and-a-half-year-olds did so three quarters of the time. Children thus know that a predicate like round applies to individual items, not to groups.","zh":"Syrett（2015）用纽扣图片测试谓语理解。孩子先看到大小、颜色、形状各异的纽扣，再看到星形纽扣摆成一颗星的轮廓。测试时，摆成圆形的三角形纽扣与摆成三角形的圆形纽扣并排出现，玩偶说：「Point to the round buttons.」三岁以上儿童稳定地指向圆形纽扣，即使两岁半的孩子也有四分之三的时候选择正确。可见儿童知道 round 这类谓语适用于个体事物，而不是一组事物。"}]},"chapter-136-slug-11-9-growing-up-bilingual-or-multilingual":{"title":{"en":"11.9 Growing up bilingual (or multilingual!)","zh":"11.9 在双语（或多语）环境中成长"},"summary":{"en":"Much of the child language literature studies monolinguals, yet growing up with two or more languages is at least as common worldwide. Because mental grammars are built from input, bilingual children receive less of each language, which can produce slight delays when measured in one language. The evidence shows no harm, possible benefits for executive function, and real value in keeping family connections.","zh":"儿童语言研究多以单语儿童为对象，但在世界范围内，同时接触两种或更多语言成长同样普遍。由于心理语法由语言输入建构，双语儿童在每种语言上获得的输入量较少，若只用单一语言衡量，发展可能略有延迟。证据表明这并无害处，反而可能有利于执行功能，并能维系与家人的联系。"},"points":[{"en":"Monolingual children are not the global norm; many children grow up with two or more languages around them.","zh":"单语儿童并非世界范围内的常态，许多儿童在两种或更多语言的环境中成长。"},{"en":"Children build a mental grammar from the input available, so less input in a language means slower development in it.","zh":"儿童依据可获得的输入建构心理语法，因此某一语言的输入较少，该语言的发展就较慢。"},{"en":"Measured in one language, bilinguals may lag slightly, but their combined vocabulary across both languages is equal or larger.","zh":"只按一种语言衡量，双语儿童可能略滞后，但两种语言合起来的总词汇量与单语儿童相当甚至更大。"},{"en":"Slight delays are within normal variation and most bilingual children catch up with monolingual peers by about age ten.","zh":"轻微滞后属于正常个体差异，多数双语儿童到十岁左右便能赶上单语同伴。"},{"en":"Advice to speak only English at home reflects power and privilege and stigma about accents, not evidence about development.","zh":"要求在家只说英语的建议反映的是权力、特权以及对口音的污名，而非发展方面的证据。"},{"en":"Evidence links bilingualism to executive function advantages and to less racial bias, though the debate continues.","zh":"有证据将双语与执行功能优势及更少的种族偏见联系起来，但相关争论仍在继续。"}],"terms":[{"en":"bilingual","zh":"双语的","defEn":"Describing a person or environment that involves two languages.","defZh":"指涉及两种语言的人或语言环境。"},{"en":"monolingual","zh":"单语的","defEn":"Describing a child or environment with only one language.","defZh":"指只使用或只接触一种语言的儿童或环境。"},{"en":"mental grammar","zh":"心理语法","defEn":"The unconscious linguistic knowledge a speaker builds from input.","defZh":"说话者依据输入建构起来的、无意识的语言知识系统。"},{"en":"input","zh":"输入","defEn":"The language a child hears or sees in the environment.","defZh":"儿童在环境中听到或看到的语言材料。"},{"en":"executive function","zh":"执行功能","defEn":"Mental processes governing attention and the control of impulses.","defZh":"支配注意力并控制冲动的心理过程。"}],"examples":[{"text":"six hours of Language A and six hours of Language B","noteEn":"The hypothetical bilingual environment, which gives less input in each language.","noteZh":"假设的双语环境，儿童在两种语言上各获得一半输入。"},{"text":"speak English at home so their child doesn’t get confused","noteEn":"Advice sometimes given to immigrant parents, based on bias rather than evidence.","noteZh":"有时给予移民家长的建议，其依据是偏见而非证据。"}],"body":[{"en":"Most child language research studies children acquiring a single language, yet monolingual children are not the norm worldwide. Growing up with more than one language is just as common: one language at home and another at daycare, different adults speaking different languages, or adults switching among two or three. In Canada and the US, where English has privileged status, bilingualism has often been treated as a disadvantage.","zh":"多数儿童语言研究考察的是只习得一种语言的儿童，但单语儿童并非世界范围内的常态。在多种语言中成长同样普遍：在家用一种语言、在日托中心用另一种；不同成人说不同语言；或成人交替使用两三种语言。在英语享有特权地位的加拿大和美国，双语常被视为一种劣势。"},{"en":"Because children build a mental grammar from the language they encounter, the quantity of input matters. Picture two children awake twelve hours a day and always exposed to language: the monolingual hears twelve hours of Language A, while the bilingual hears, say, six hours of A and six of B. Measured in one language, a bilingual may therefore have a slightly smaller vocabulary and reach grammatical milestones a little later (Hoff et al., 2011). Across both languages, however, total vocabulary is the same or larger than a monolingual’s at the same age (Hoff et al., 2014).","zh":"由于儿童依据所接触的语言建构心理语法，输入量十分重要。设想两个孩子每天醒着十二小时且始终接触语言：单语儿童听到十二小时的语言 A，双语儿童则听到比如六小时 A 和六小时 B。若只按一种语言衡量，双语儿童的词汇量可能略小，达到语法里程碑也稍晚（Hoff 等，2011）。但把两种语言合起来，其总词汇量与同龄单语儿童相当甚至更大（Hoff 等，2014）。"},{"en":"Language acquisition is not a race, and a few weeks’ difference is no cause for concern. Children and environments vary widely; some research places the delay within the normal range for monolinguals, and much of it suggests that most bilingual children catch up in both languages by about age ten. Pressure on immigrant families to speak English at home reflects power, privilege and the stigma attached to non-English languages and accents rather than children’s development.","zh":"语言习得不是比赛，相差几周并不值得担忧。儿童与语言环境的差异很大，有研究认为这种延迟仍在单语儿童的正常变异范围内，也有研究显示多数双语儿童到十岁左右会在两种语言上赶上。要求移民家庭在家说英语的压力，反映的是权力、特权以及加在非英语语言和口音上的污名，而非儿童发展的需要。"},{"en":"The evidence shows no harm and some advantages. Bilinguals tend to score higher on executive function, the processes governing attention and impulse control, perhaps because they constantly suppress one language while using the other, though researchers still debate these effects (Bialystok, 2009; Valian, 2015). Bilingual 14-month-olds remain surprised by uncooperative unfamiliar speech, while monolinguals do not (Colomer & Sebastian-Galles, 2020), and bilingual toddlers show less racial bias (Singh, Quinn, et al., 2020). Most importantly, bilingualism preserves relationships with grandparents.","zh":"证据表明双语并无害处，反而有一些优势。双语者在执行功能（即支配注意力、抑制冲动的心理过程）上得分往往更高，这或许是因为他们使用一种语言时不断抑制另一种语言，但研究者对这些效应仍有争论（Bialystok，2009；Valian，2015）。14 个月大的双语婴儿面对用陌生语言进行的不合作行为仍会惊讶，单语婴儿则不会（Colomer 与 Sebastian-Galles，2020）；双语幼儿的种族偏见也更少（Singh、Quinn 等，2020）。最重要的是，双语让儿童得以与祖辈保持联系。"}]},"chapter-137-slug-11-10-language-milestones-in-the-first-two-years":{"title":{"en":"11.10 Language milestones in the first two years","zh":"11.10 生命头两年的语言里程碑"},"summary":{"en":"This section presents a table of typical language milestones from before birth to age 2;0. It covers hearing fetuses responding to the pregnant parent’s voice, babbling with syllable structure, first words, phoneme categorization, word comprehension, two- and three-word utterances, and the use of syntactic structure to interpret novel words and verbs. The section stresses that children vary immensely and that language learning is not a race.","zh":"本节以表格列出从出生前到 2;0 的典型语言发展里程碑，包括胎儿对孕母声音的反应、具有音节结构的咿呀语、首批词、音位范畴化、词汇理解、两三个词的语句，以及依据句法结构解读新词和新动词等。本节强调儿童之间差异极大，语言学习不是比赛。"},"points":[{"en":"Before birth, hearing fetuses already respond differently to the pregnant parent’s voice than to other voices.","zh":"出生前，有听力的胎儿对孕母的声音就已表现出与其他声音不同的反应。"},{"en":"At 0;6 babies notice differences in handshapes or speech segments and begin rhythmic babbling with syllable structure.","zh":"在 0;6，婴儿能注意到手形或语音音段的差异，并开始发出带音节结构、有节奏的咿呀语。"},{"en":"Sign-acquiring babies produce first words around 0;9, while speech-acquiring babies do so around 1;0.","zh":"习得手语的婴儿约在 0;9 说出首批词，习得口语的婴儿约在 1;0 说出首批词。"},{"en":"Around 1;0 babies categorize segments into the phoneme categories of the ambient language and understand about ten words.","zh":"约在 1;0，婴儿能把音段归入周围语言的音位范畴，并理解约十个常用词。"},{"en":"Between 1;2 and 2;0 children use syntactic category, structure and frames to interpret novel words and verbs.","zh":"在 1;2 到 2;0 之间，儿童利用句法类别、结构和框架来解读新词与新动词。"}],"terms":[{"en":"milestone","zh":"里程碑","defEn":"A typical developmental achievement used to track children’s progress.","defZh":"用于追踪儿童发展进程的典型发展成就。"},{"en":"babbling","zh":"咿呀语","defEn":"Rhythmically produced early vocalizations that have syllable structure.","defZh":"婴儿早期发出的、具有音节结构且富有节奏的语音。"},{"en":"prosody","zh":"韵律","defEn":"The rhythm, stress and intonation patterns of spoken language.","defZh":"口语中的节奏、重音和语调模式。"},{"en":"ambient language","zh":"周围语言","defEn":"The language or languages present in a child’s environment.","defZh":"儿童所处环境中出现的语言。"},{"en":"syntactic frame","zh":"句法框架","defEn":"The sentence structure surrounding a word that helps guide interpretation.","defZh":"围绕某个词的句子结构，可帮助推断其意义。"}],"examples":[{"text":"respond differently to pregnant parent’s voice than other voices (hearing fetuses only).","noteEn":"The earliest milestone in the table, before birth, limited to hearing fetuses.","noteZh":"表中最早的里程碑，出现在出生前，仅适用于有听力的胎儿。"},{"text":"begin to produce rhythmic babbling with syllable structure.","noteEn":"Babbling at 0;6 already shows the organization of syllables.","noteZh":"到 0;6，咿呀语已表现出音节的组织方式。"},{"text":"produce utterances of two or three words.","noteEn":"At 1;6, early multi-word speech appears alongside comprehension of about 50 words.","noteZh":"1;6 时出现早期多词语句，同时能理解约五十个词。"},{"text":"interpret meanings for novel verbs depending on syntactic frames.","noteEn":"At 2;0 children use sentence structure as a clue to verb meaning.","noteZh":"到 2;0，儿童把句子结构当作推断动词意义的线索。"}],"body":[{"en":"The table in this section collects some typical language development milestones of the first two years of life. Even before birth, hearing fetuses respond differently to the pregnant parent’s voice than to other voices, and hearing newborns respond differently to the prosody of that spoken language than to another language. By 0;6, sighted infants notice differences in handshapes and hearing infants notice differences in speech segments, and babies begin to produce rhythmic babbling that already has syllable structure.","zh":"本节表格汇总了生命头两年的一些典型语言发展里程碑。早在出生前，有听力的胎儿对孕母声音的反应就不同于对其他声音的反应；有听力的新生儿对该口语的韵律反应也不同于对另一种语言的反应。到 0;6，视力正常的婴儿能注意到手形差异，有听力的婴儿能注意到语音音段的差异，并开始发出已具备音节结构、富有节奏的咿呀语。"},{"en":"The milestones then move from production to comprehension and to the use of grammar. Sign-acquiring babies produce their first words around 0;9 and speech-acquiring babies around 1;0. At about 1;0 children categorize phonetically different segments into the phoneme categories of the ambient language and understand the meanings of roughly ten common words. Later, at 1;2 they interpret novel words differently depending on syntactic category, at 1;3 they assign compositional meaning depending on syntactic structure, and at 1;6 they produce two- or three-word utterances and understand about 50 words. By 2;0 they interpret novel verbs using syntactic frames and ask questions. The section reminds us that children vary immensely and that nearly every child with appropriate access to other humans using language will develop a mental grammar in due time.","zh":"这些里程碑随后从产出转向理解，再转向语法的运用。习得手语的婴儿约在 0;9 说出首批词，习得口语的婴儿约在 1;0 说出首批词。约 1;0 时，儿童能把语音上不同的音段归入周围语言的音位范畴，并理解约十个常用词的意义。此后，1;2 时他们会依据句法类别对生词作不同解读，1;3 时依据句法结构赋予组合性意义，1;6 时能说出两三个词的语句并理解约五十个词。到 2;0，他们能借助句法框架解读生疏动词的意义，并会提问。本节提醒我们，儿童之间差异极大，只要能够适当接触使用语言的其他人类，几乎所有儿童都会在适当时候发展出心理语法。"}]},"chapter-138-slug-11-11-exercise-your-linguistics-skills":{"title":{"en":"11.11 Exercise your linguistics skills","zh":"11.11 锻炼你的语言学技能"},"summary":{"en":"Three exercises apply the chapter’s ideas. The first asks students to compare children’s unusual uses of words, reported by Bowerman (1988), with adult grammar. The second uses an elicitation experiment by Ambridge et al. (2006) on wh-questions, asking for a tree diagram of the adult form and a comparison with children’s errors. The third asks students to analyse the power structures and biases behind a teacher’s advice that an immigrant family speak English at home.","zh":"本节三道练习运用本章所学。第一题要求比较 Bowerman（1988）所记录儿童对词语的不寻常用法与成人语法。第二题依据 Ambridge 等（2006）关于 wh-问句的诱发实验，要求为成人的问句画出树形图，并与儿童的错误作比较。第三题要求分析教师建议移民家庭在家说英语这一做法背后的权力结构与偏见。"},"points":[{"en":"Exercise 1 compares a child’s unusual word use with the word’s category in adult grammar.","zh":"练习一比较儿童不寻常的用词与该词在成人语法中的词类。"},{"en":"Children used nouns like button and cough as verbs, and the adjective comfortable as a verb.","zh":"儿童把 button、cough 等名词当动词用，把形容词 comfortable 也当动词用。"},{"en":"Exercise 2 examines wh-question errors: missing inversion and a doubled auxiliary.","zh":"练习二考察 wh-问句错误：缺少主谓倒装，以及助动词重复。"},{"en":"Exercise 3 asks what power structures and biases shape advice to drop a home language.","zh":"练习三追问：是什么样的权力结构与偏见塑造了放弃家庭语言的建议。"},{"en":"Students should draw a tree diagram of the adult question and compare it with the children’s errors.","zh":"学生应为成人的问句画出树形图，并与儿童错误句作比较。"}],"terms":[{"en":"elicitation experiment","zh":"诱发实验","defEn":"A task designed to prompt children to produce a particular structure.","defZh":"旨在引导儿童产出特定结构的实验任务。"},{"en":"wh-question","zh":"wh-问句","defEn":"A question formed with a wh-word such as what or who.","defZh":"用 what、who 等 wh-词构成的问句。"},{"en":"inversion","zh":"倒装","defEn":"The placement of the auxiliary before the subject in questions.","defZh":"问句中把助动词置于主语之前的操作。"},{"en":"tree diagram","zh":"树形图","defEn":"A branching representation of the syntactic structure of a sentence.","defZh":"用分支方式表示句子句法结构的图形。"},{"en":"subcategory","zh":"次类","defEn":"A narrower class within a lexical category, such as transitive verb.","defZh":"词类内部更细的分类，如及物动词。"}],"examples":[{"text":"Button me the rest.","noteEn":"The child uses a noun where adult grammar requires a verb.","noteZh":"儿童把名词用在成人语法要求动词的位置上。"},{"text":"They just cough me.","noteEn":"Another noun used verbally, showing an unusual subcategory.","noteZh":"又一名词被当动词使用，显示出异常的次类。"},{"text":"I want to comfortable you.","noteEn":"The adjective comfortable appears in a verb position.","noteZh":"形容词 comfortable 出现在动词的位置上。"},{"text":"What they are drinking?","noteEn":"A child wh-question lacking the required subject-auxiliary inversion.","noteZh":"儿童 wh-问句中缺少必需的主语—助动词倒装。"}],"body":[{"en":"The first exercise presents utterances by young children reported by Bowerman (1988) and asks the student to describe each bolded word’s category or subcategory in adult grammar, then compare the child’s use with it. The child says Button me the rest, They just cough me, and I want to comfortable you. In each case the word is used in a way that is unusual relative to adult English grammar, so the task is to work out what category the word belongs to for adults and how the child’s grammar differs.","zh":"第一题给出 Bowerman（1988）记录的幼儿话语，要求学生说明每个黑体词在成人语法中的词类或次类，再比较儿童的用法与之有何不同。儿童说的话包括 Button me the rest、They just cough me 和 I want to comfortable you。这些词的使用方式相对于成人英语语法都不寻常，因此任务是弄清这些词在成人语法中属于什么词类，以及儿童的语法有何差异。"},{"en":"The second exercise draws on an elicitation experiment by Ambridge et al. (2006) on preschool children’s production of wh-questions. The researcher tells the child that Mickey and Minnie are drinking something, says I wonder what they are drinking, and then asks the child to ask the dog what they are drinking. Children often answer with an adult-like What are they drinking?, but sometimes produce errors such as What they are drinking? or What are they are drinking?. Students must draw a tree diagram for the adult question and compare the children’s grammars with it, using the errors as evidence of how those grammars differ.","zh":"第二题取材于 Ambridge 等（2006）关于学前儿童 wh-问句产出的诱发实验。研究者先告诉儿童 Mickey and Minnie are drinking something，接着说 I wonder what they are drinking，然后让儿童去问小狗它们在喝什么。儿童常给出与成人相近的 What are they drinking?，但有时也会说出 What they are drinking? 或 What are they are drinking? 这类错误。学生需为成人的问句画出树形图，并以这些错误为证据，比较儿童语法与成人语法的差异。"},{"en":"The third exercise is a scenario for reflection rather than data analysis. A cousin’s child starts kindergarten at age 3;10, having spent half-days in an English-language daycare and the rest of the time at home with parents and grandparents who mostly speak Farsi. At the first parent-teacher interview the teacher says the child is behind on some typical milestones and advises the parents to speak English at home. Students are asked what power structures are at play in that advice, what biases the teacher holds, and what advice they could give their cousin, informed by what they know about language acquisition and about power and privilege.","zh":"第三题是一个用于反思而非数据分析的情境。表亲的孩子 3;10 开始上幼儿园，此前半天在英语日托中心度过，其余时间在家与父母和祖父母相处，家中成人大多说波斯语。第一次家长会上，教师指出孩子在某些典型里程碑上落后于其他儿童，并建议家长在家说英语。题目要求学生思考：这一建议背后有哪些权力结构在起作用，教师持有什么偏见，以及依据语言习得、权力与特权的知识，他们可以给表亲提出什么建议。"}]},"part-012-chapter-12-adult-language-learning":{"title":{"en":"Chapter 12: Adult Language Learning","zh":"第 12 章：成人语言学习"},"summary":{"en":"Many linguistics students already know more than one language, and the metalinguistic awareness that comes with bilingualism or language learning often draws them to the field. Chapter 11 examined how humans acquire language from birth; this chapter turns to learning a language after the first one, outlining the differences, motivations, challenges, and typical processes involved.","zh":"许多语言学学生本身就不止掌握一种语言，双语、多语或语言学习带来的元语言意识往往正是他们被语言学吸引的原因。第 11 章考察人类如何从出生起习得语言，本章则转向第一种语言之后的语言学习，概述其中的差异、动机、挑战与常见过程。"},"points":[{"en":"Adult language learning differs from acquiring a language from birth in several key ways.","zh":"成人语言学习与从出生起习得语言在若干关键方面存在差异。"},{"en":"Learners of additional languages have varied motivations and face varied challenges.","zh":"额外语言的学习者动机各异，所面对的挑战也各不相同。"},{"en":"Certain processes are typical of learning any language as an adult.","zh":"有些过程是成人学习任何语言时都会出现的典型现象。"},{"en":"A learner's first language can shape how they learn an additional language.","zh":"学习者的第一语言会影响其学习额外语言的方式。"}],"terms":[{"en":"metalinguistic awareness","zh":"元语言意识","defEn":"the ability to reflect consciously on language as an object.","defZh":"有意识地反思语言本身、把语言当作对象来思考的能力。"},{"en":"bilingualism","zh":"双语现象","defEn":"the regular use of two languages by an individual or community.","defZh":"个人或社群经常使用两种语言的状态。"},{"en":"multilingualism","zh":"多语现象","defEn":"the regular use of three or more languages.","defZh":"经常使用三种或更多语言的状态。"}],"examples":[],"body":[{"en":"Students of linguistics frequently arrive with more than one language already in hand, and it is often the metalinguistic awareness accompanying bilingualism, multilingualism, or earlier language learning that first attracted them to the discipline. Where Chapter 11 asked how humans acquire language from birth, this chapter asks a different question: how do we learn a language once a first one is already established?","zh":"学习语言学的人往往已经掌握不止一种语言，而伴随双语、多语或以往语言学习而来的元语言意识，常常正是最初吸引他们进入这一学科的原因。第 11 章追问的是人类如何从出生起习得语言，本章则提出另一个问题：当第一种语言已经建立之后，我们又是如何学习一门语言的？"},{"en":"The chapter sets out four learning goals. Readers should be able to discuss how learning a language as an adult differs from acquiring one from birth, to understand some motivations and challenges of learning an additional language, to identify processes typical of adult learning of any language, and to predict how a learner's first language may affect the learning of a later one.","zh":"本章提出四项学习目标：能够讨论成人学习语言与从出生起习得语言有何不同；能够理解学习额外语言的一些动机与挑战；能够识别成人学习任何语言时都典型的过程；能够预测学习者的第一语言会如何影响后续语言的学习。"},{"en":"These goals frame the units that follow, which move from cognitive, linguistic, and socioemotional differences between adults and children to the varied reasons adults take up a later language.","zh":"这些目标框定了随后的单元：先讨论成人与儿童在认知、语言和社会情感方面的差异，再讨论成人学习后续语言的各种原因。"},{"en":"These goals frame the two units that follow, which move from the differences between adults and children to the varied reasons adults take up a later language, such as migration, employment, education, cultural enrichment, and community connection.","zh":"这些目标框定了随后的两个单元：先讨论成人与儿童之间的差异，再讨论成人学习后续语言的各种原因，如移民、就业、教育、文化充实与社群联结。"}]},"chapter-139-slug-12-1-adults-are-not-children":{"title":{"en":"12.1 Adults are not children","zh":"12.1 成人不是儿童"},"summary":{"en":"Textbooks usually call this subfield Second Language Acquisition (SLA), but that label assumes a learner knows exactly one language already and that the next one is therefore second, an assumption that is narrow and Anglocentric. This unit proposes L1 or first language and later language instead, then compares adults with children in cognitive, linguistic, and socioemotional terms.","zh":"教科书通常把这一分支称为第二语言习得（SLA），但这一标签预设学习者已精通且仅精通一种语言、下一门语言因此是第二语言，这种预设既狭窄又以英语世界为中心。本单元改用 L1 或第一语言与后续语言的说法，并从认知、语言和社会情感三个方面比较成人与儿童。"},"points":[{"en":"The term SLA wrongly assumes the learner already has exactly one language.","zh":"第二语言习得这一术语错误地预设学习者已恰好掌握一种语言。"},{"en":"About one-third of the world's people use two languages regularly.","zh":"世界上约有三分之一的人经常使用两种语言。"},{"en":"Terms like foreign language and ESL reveal the field's Anglocentrism.","zh":"外语、英语作为第二语言等说法暴露出该领域的英语中心倾向。"},{"en":"Adults have less neural plasticity, so learning takes more effort.","zh":"成人的神经可塑性较低，因此学习需要付出更多努力。"},{"en":"Adults can draw on metacognitive skills and metalinguistic awareness.","zh":"成人可以运用元认知技能和元语言意识。"},{"en":"Self-consciousness and socioemotional factors can also hinder adults.","zh":"自我意识和社恐等社会情感因素也会妨碍成人学习。"}],"terms":[{"en":"Second Language Acquisition (SLA)","zh":"第二语言习得","defEn":"the subfield of linguistics that studies adult language learning.","defZh":"语言学的分支领域，研究成人的语言学习。"},{"en":"L1","zh":"第一语言","defEn":"any language learned from early childhood, even more than one at once.","defZh":"任何从幼儿期习得的语言，即使同时习得不止一种。"},{"en":"later language","zh":"后续语言","defEn":"any language learned after the first one or ones.","defZh":"在第一种（或几种）语言之后习得的任何语言。"},{"en":"neural plasticity","zh":"神经可塑性","defEn":"the brain's readiness to form new connections from experience.","defZh":"大脑根据经验建立新神经连接的灵敏程度。"},{"en":"metacognitive skills","zh":"元认知技能","defEn":"conscious strategies for managing and monitoring one's own learning.","defZh":"有意识地管理和监控自身学习过程的策略。"},{"en":"metalinguistic awareness","zh":"元语言意识","defEn":"the ability to consciously reflect on and analyse language.","defZh":"有意识地反思和分析语言的能力。"}],"examples":[],"body":[{"en":"Most introductory textbooks would title this chapter Second Language Acquisition (SLA), the usual name for the subfield studying adult language learning. That label assumes the typical learner is proficient in exactly one language, acquired natively, so whatever comes next must be the second. The assumption is narrow: about one third of the world's people use two languages regularly, and many use three or more (Wei, 2007).","zh":"多数入门教科书会把本章命名为第二语言习得（SLA），这是研究成人语言学习这一分支的常用名称。这个标签预设典型学习者恰好精通一种从幼年自然习得的语言，因此接下来学的必然是第二种。这一预设相当狭窄：全世界约三分之一的人经常使用两种语言，其中许多人还使用三种或更多（Wei, 2007）。"},{"en":"The same assumption sits inside English as a Second Language (ESL). Some teachers say additional language instead, and so-called foreign languages are now often called world languages. As Chapter 2 showed, few terms are truly neutral. This chapter uses L1, or first language, for anything learned from early childhood, and later language for anything learned afterwards. One key difference from first language learning is that you already have a mental grammar when you begin another; the other is that adults are not children.","zh":"同样的预设也存在于英语作为第二语言（ESL）这一说法中。有些教师改用额外语言，而所谓的外语如今常被称作世界语言。正如第 2 章所示，真正中立的术语少之又少。本章用 L1 或第一语言指称任何从幼儿期习得的语言，用后续语言指称之后习得的语言。与第一语言学习相比，一个关键差别是你在开始学另一门语言时已经拥有一个心理语法；另一个差别是成人不是儿童。"},{"en":"Children learn language quickly and without much effort as long as adult language is available, partly because of neural plasticity: their brains eagerly build new connections from experience. For older learners, new neural pathways are harder to grow, so learning takes more effort, though it is far from impossible. Adults hold advantages too. We can apply metacognitive skills, memorizing vocabulary and morphology or seeking out books, movies and podcasts, and we can use metalinguistic awareness, practicing new articulator positions or comparing structures with our L1.","zh":"只要有机会接触成人使用的语言，儿童就能迅速而毫不费力地学会，部分原因在于神经可塑性：他们的大脑乐于根据经验建立新连接。年龄较大的学习者较难长出新的神经通路，因此学习需要更多努力，尽管绝非不可能。成人也有优势：我们可以运用元认知技能，背诵词汇和形态，或寻找书籍、电影和播客；我们还能运用元语言意识，练习发音器官的新位置，或比较新语言与母语的结构。"},{"en":"Adults also face self-consciousness. Learning a language usually means interacting with more proficient people, and for an adult used to being seen as competent, feeling like a beginner and making mistakes can be embarrassing. The subfield has often focused narrowly on grammar, especially phonetics, morphology and syntax, an approach tied to colonial thinking that treats language as an object separable from people and communities. Yet our use of language is interwoven with emotions and identities, and adult learners bring cultural knowledge and emotions they may not fully recognize.","zh":"成人还要面对自我意识的问题。学习一门语言通常意味着与更熟练的人互动，而对一个习惯被看作能干的人来说，感到自己像初学者、不断犯错会令人难堪。这一分支常常只盯着语法，尤其是语音、形态和句法，这种取向与殖民式思维有关，把语言当作可以脱离人和社群的物品。然而我们对语言的使用与情感和身份交织在一起，成人学习者带着各种文化知识和情绪进入学习，而他们未必都能意识到这些。"}]},"chapter-140-slug-12-2-motivations-for-adult-language-learning":{"title":{"en":"12.2 Motivations for adult language learners","zh":"12.2 成人语言学习者的动机"},"summary":{"en":"Infants cannot help learning whatever language surrounds them, but adults learn for many different reasons, and those reasons shape how they learn. This unit examines three broad motivations: migration, employment and education; cultural enrichment; and community connection, especially the reclamation of Indigenous languages and the barriers and health benefits associated with it.","zh":"婴儿无法不去学习周围的语言，而成人学习语言的原因多种多样，这些原因又影响着他们学习的方式。本单元考察三类主要动机：移民、就业与教育；文化充实；以及社群联结，尤其是原住民语言的 reclaim（重拾），及其伴随的障碍与健康收益。"},"points":[{"en":"Adult learners have many different motivations, unlike infants, and these shape their learning.","zh":"与婴儿不同，成人学习者动机多样，而这些动机塑造了他们的学习方式。"},{"en":"Economic migration creates a clear motivation to learn English in Canada.","zh":"出于经济目的的移民在加拿大有明确的英语学习动机。"},{"en":"ESL teaching often rests on prescriptive, racist and colonial assumptions about correctness.","zh":"ESL 教学常常建立在关于正确性的规定式、种族主义与殖民式预设之上。"},{"en":"World language curricula often assume a white English-speaking learner.","zh":"世界语言课程常常预设学习者是讲英语的白人。"},{"en":"Indigenous adults reclaim their languages for Elders' teachings and for their children.","zh":"原住民成人重拾本族语言，是为了长老的教诲，也是为了自己的孩子。"},{"en":"Higher language proficiency correlates with lower diabetes and youth suicide rates.","zh":"较高的语言熟练度与较低的糖尿病率和青少年自杀率相关。"}],"terms":[{"en":"standard language ideologies","zh":"标准语言意识形态","defEn":"beliefs that treat one prescribed variety as the only correct one.","defZh":"把某一种规定性变体视为唯一正确形式的观念。"},{"en":"raciolinguistic stigma","zh":"种族语言污名","defEn":"stigmatizing people's speech in ways tied to race and appearance.","defZh":"与种族和外貌相关联、针对他人言语的污名化。"},{"en":"language reclamation","zh":"语言重拾","defEn":"reviving a language and its connections to community and land.","defZh":"复兴一门语言及其与社群、土地之间联系的工作。"},{"en":"survivance","zh":"存续抵抗","defEn":"blending survival of a language with resistance to colonial oppression.","defZh":"把语言的存续与对殖民压迫的抵抗结合起来。"},{"en":"bound morpheme","zh":"黏着语素","defEn":"a morpheme that cannot stand alone and must attach to another.","defZh":"不能单独出现、必须附着于其他成分的语素。"},{"en":"multi-generational trauma","zh":"代际创伤","defEn":"trauma passed down through generations, here about language.","defZh":"在代际之间传递的创伤，此处特指与语言相关者。"}],"examples":[{"text":"–aatawee–","noteEn":"The myaamia verb meaning 'to speak a language', a bound morpheme.","noteZh":"myaamia 语中表示“说一门语言”的动词，是黏着语素。"},{"text":"the verb –aatawee– “can’t stand alone; we have to attach it to the people” (Leonard, 2017, p. 30)","noteEn":"A myaamia speaker links the bound verb to community and people.","noteZh":"一位 myaamia 语使用者把这个黏着动词与社群和人联系起来。"},{"text":"Oster et al. (2014)’s quantitative analysis of 31 First Nations in Alberta showed that the Nations with higher language proficiency had lower rates of diabetes.","noteEn":"Evidence linking language proficiency with community health outcomes.","noteZh":"把语言熟练度与社群健康结果联系起来的一项证据。"},{"text":"Hallett et al. (2007) found that the communities with the highest numbers of speakers of the language had the lowest suicide rates among youth.","noteEn":"A British Columbia finding on speakers and youth suicide rates.","noteZh":"不列颠哥伦比亚省关于语言使用者数量与青少年自杀率的发现。"}],"body":[{"en":"Infant learners cannot help learning whatever language surrounds them, so asking about their motivation is pointless. Adults take up a language for many reasons, and those reasons shape how they learn. Migration, employment and education give one clear case: many Canadian employers expect proficiency in English, so people who immigrate for work or school have an obvious economic motivation. Too often, however, courses for adults rest on standard language ideologies with racist and colonialist assumptions, treating English as a fixed asset contained in textbooks.","zh":"婴儿只要有语言输入就必然学会，追问其动机没有意义。成人学习语言的动机多种多样，而这些动机塑造了他们的学习方式。移民、就业与教育是明显的一类：加拿大许多雇主都要求精通英语，为工作或学业移民的人因此有明确的经济动机。但成人英语课程往往建立在带有种族主义与殖民主义预设的标准语言意识形态之上，把英语当作教科书里的固定资产。"},{"en":"Swift (2022) argues that the language students saw and heard seemed designed to represent prescriptive norms rather than believable examples of real-life practice, with the teacher as the ultimate arbiter of correctness; Ramjattan (2019b) shows white people are perceived as better teachers than people of colour. Rosa and Flores (2021) note that prescriptivism is usually meant benevolently, but even linguistic practices matching mainstream standards kept being perceived as deficient and in need of remediation (2021, p. 1164), and listeners' perception of a foreign accent depends on the speaker's appearance as much as on their speech (Babel & Russell, 2015).","zh":"Swift（2022）指出，学生看到和听到的语言似乎意在呈现规定性规范，而非真实生活的可信示例，教师则成为正确性的最终裁决者；Ramjattan（2019b）表明，白人被认为比有色人种更适合当老师。Rosa 与 Flores（2021）指出，规定式教学通常出于善意，但即使语言实践符合主流标准，也仍被视为有缺陷、需要补救（2021, p. 1164），而听者对外国口音的感知既取决于言语，也同样取决于说话人的外貌（Babel & Russell, 2015）。"},{"en":"A second motivation is cultural enrichment: learning another culture can expand one's worldview, with incentives of travel, exchange or a semester abroad. Such languages were once called foreign languages, implying that anything not English is foreign. Curricular materials nonetheless tend to assume a white English-speaking learner. Anya (2021) showed that college Spanish curricula in the USA systematically excluded Black learners, disregarding African-American cultural occasions and news and even omitting vocabulary for describing African descendants' appearance.","zh":"第二种动机是文化充实：了解另一种文化可以拓展世界观，还有旅行、交换项目或海外学期的激励。这类语言过去被称为外语，隐含凡非英语者皆为外来之意。然而课程与教材仍倾向于预设学习者是以英语为母语的白人。Anya（2021）表明，美国大学西班牙语课程系统性地排斥黑人学习者：既忽视非裔美国人的文化节日与新闻，连描述非洲裔外貌的词汇也没有恰当说法。"},{"en":"A third motivation, community connection, concerns the Indigenous languages of North America, which the colonial Canadian government worked systematically and often violently to eradicate. Learning their Nation's language as an adult is therefore vitally important for many Indigenous people denied that chance in childhood: it allows a connection with their Elders' stories and teachings, and many strive for enough proficiency that their children can learn the language at home. Ferguson and Weaselboy (2020) argue that land must be experienced through Indigenous language to appreciate its layers of meaning, and Davis (2017) calls reclamation work survivance.","zh":"第三种动机是社群联结，涉及北美原住民语言；殖民时期的加拿大政府曾系统性地、往往以暴力手段铲除这些语言。因此，对许多童年时被剥夺学习机会的原住民来说，以成人身份学习本民族的语言至关重要：这让他们与长老的故事和教诲相连，许多人努力达到足够熟练度，好让孩子在家里学会这门语言。Ferguson 与 Weaselboy（2020）主张，必须通过原住民语言体验土地，才能领会其中的层层含义；Davis（2017）把重拾语言称为存续抵抗。"},{"en":"One myaamia speaker made the point through morphology: the verb –aatawee– cannot stand alone and must be attached to the people (Leonard, 2017, p. 30). Learners also face particular barriers: few chances to practice, because speakers and materials are scarce, and multi-generational trauma about their languages from colonial schools (McIvor, 2020). Universities built on Euro-Western colonial ideals may not be the right venue; the University of Victoria programme aims to respond to the needs expressed by First Nations community partners.","zh":"一位 myaamia 语使用者用形态学说明了这一点：动词 –aatawee– 不能单独存在，必须附着于人（Leonard, 2017, p. 30）。学习者还面临特殊障碍：使用者和材料稀少、练习机会有限，而且常因殖民学校的经历背负与语言相关的代际创伤（McIvor, 2020）。建立在欧美殖民理想之上的大学未必合适；维多利亚大学的语言项目力求回应原住民社群伙伴的需求。"},{"en":"Yet some learners report substantial mental and physical health benefits as they gain proficiency. Oster et al. (2014) found that Alberta First Nations with higher language proficiency had lower rates of diabetes, and Hallett et al. (2007) found that British Columbia communities with the most speakers had the lowest youth suicide rates. These results should not be read as grammar causing good health; they align with what Elders say about the deep connections between their languages and their cultures.","zh":"不过，一些学习者在提高熟练度的过程中报告了显著的身心健康收益。Oster 等（2014）发现，语言熟练度较高的阿尔伯塔原住民族群糖尿病发病率较低；Hallett 等（2007）发现，使用者最多的不列颠哥伦比亚社群青少年自杀率最低。这些结果不应被解读为语法带来健康，而是与长老们关于语言和本族文化深层联系的说法相呼应。"}]},"chapter-141-slug-12-3-gaining-proficiency":{"title":{"en":"12.3 Gaining proficiency","zh":"12.3 达到熟练水平"},"summary":{"en":"Fluency and proficiency are not neutral facts but judgements shaped by standardization. Canada and the United States publish detailed benchmarks that rank learners, and scale labels such as Superior imply that other users are inferior. For Indigenous languages the question is harder still, because definitions depend on colonial documentation, yet benchmarks can also serve reawakening programs. Ultimately learners themselves decide what counts as proficient.","zh":"流利与熟练并非中立的事实，而是受标准化影响的判断。加拿大和美国都发布了详尽的能力基准，对学习者分级；Superior（高级）这类量表名称本身就在暗示另一些使用者是低劣的。对原住民语言而言，问题更为复杂：定义依赖殖民时期的文献记录，但基准也能服务于语言复兴项目。归根结底，什么算熟练由学习者自己决定。"},"points":[{"en":"Building another grammar as an adult takes enormous effort and practice, and many learners never feel fully fluent.","zh":"成年后建构另一套语法需要巨大的努力与练习，许多学习者始终觉得自己不够流利。"},{"en":"Like all standardization, official proficiency benchmarks rank learners and carry implicit value judgements.","zh":"与一切标准化一样，官方能力基准对学习者分级，并暗含价值判断。"},{"en":"Naming the top level Superior automatically implies that other language users are inferior, feeding accent prejudice.","zh":"把最高等级命名为高级，就自动暗示其他语言使用者低劣，从而助长口音偏见。"},{"en":"For Indigenous languages, defining fluency is complicated because colonial linguists wrote the documentation.","zh":"对原住民语言来说，流利度的定义之所以复杂，是因为文献由殖民时期的语言学家撰写。"},{"en":"Some reawakening programs nonetheless adopt published benchmarks as concrete goals for learners.","zh":"尽管如此，一些语言复兴项目仍采用已发布的基准作为学习者的具体目标。"},{"en":"Since learners do the work themselves, they get to decide what counts as proficient for their own purposes.","zh":"既然学习由学习者自己付出努力，他们就该按自己的目的来界定什么算熟练。"}],"terms":[{"en":"fluency","zh":"流利度","defEn":"The ability to use a language easily and effectively, often defined by standards.","defZh":"轻松有效地使用语言的能力，其判定往往依据某种标准。"},{"en":"benchmark","zh":"基准","defEn":"A published standard describing levels of proficiency in a language.","defZh":"官方发布、用于描述语言能力等级的标准。"},{"en":"standardized variety","zh":"标准变体","defEn":"The socially higher-status variety with more grammar books and dictionaries.","defZh":"社会地位更高、拥有更多语法书和词典的语言变体。"},{"en":"language reawakening","zh":"语言复兴（语言唤醒）","defEn":"Work that brings a dormant language back into regular use.","defZh":"使休眠语言重新恢复日常使用的工作。"},{"en":"colonialism","zh":"殖民主义","defEn":"Domination in which socially dominant groups claim the right to define valid knowledge.","defZh":"社会主导群体宣称有权界定何为有效知识的支配关系。"}],"examples":[{"text":"Benchmarks","noteEn":"Canada publishes these for English and French proficiency in the two official languages.","noteZh":"加拿大为两种官方语言的英语、法语能力发布的基准。"},{"text":"Proficiency Guidelines","noteEn":"ACTFL’s five-level scale, whose two highest levels are named Superior and Distinguished.","noteZh":"ACTFL 的五级量表，其中最高两级分别命名为高级与卓异。"},{"text":"Onkwawenna Kentyohkwa","noteEn":"A Kanyen’kéha school that sets benchmarks as goals for its learners.","noteZh":"一所 Kanyen’kéha 语学校，以能力基准作为学习者的目标。"}],"body":[{"en":"Learning a language as an adult is a great deal of work, and many later learners feel they never reach the fluency they hoped for. This section asks whether that notion of fluency is itself problematic: who decides what counts as fluent? Adult language learning is bound up with language standards, and a standardized variety is not better than others, only higher in status and richer in grammar books.","zh":"成年后学习一门语言非常费力，许多后学语言者觉得自己始终没能达到期望的流利程度。本节追问：流利这一概念本身是否就有问题？由谁来决定什么算流利？成人语言学习与语言标准紧密交织，而标准变体并不比别的变体更好，只是社会地位更高、附带的语法书和词典更多。"},{"en":"Language teachers normally see their job as helping adults meet the standard, and governments publish detailed scales. Canada issues Benchmarks for English and French defining Basic, Intermediate and Advanced proficiency in listening, speaking, reading and writing, while the American Council on the Teaching of Foreign Languages publishes Proficiency Guidelines with five levels, the top two named Superior and Distinguished. The value judgement sits in the name: labelling some users superior implies that others are inferior, which is how accent prejudice arises.","zh":"语言教师通常把工作理解为帮助成年人达到标准，政府也会发布详尽的量表。加拿大为英语和法语发布基准，界定听、说、读、写的基本、中级和高级能力；美国外语教学委员会发布五级能力指南，最高两级命名为高级（Superior）与卓异（Distinguished）。价值判断就在名称中：把某些使用者标为高级，就暗示另一些低劣，口音偏见由此产生。"},{"en":"For Indigenous languages the notion of fluency is more tangled. Learners often want to use the language in a way consistent with its traditional form, yet any language in regular use inevitably changes. Megan Lukaniec, working with archival documents to reawaken Wendat, describes both a pressure to remain true to the documented language and a freedom to forge a new path for it. Wesley Leonard, reawakening the sleeping myaamia language, notes the irony that those documents reenact colonial power by asserting the right to define valid knowledge.","zh":"对原住民语言来说，流利的含义更为纠结。学习者往往希望按传统的形态使用语言，但任何处于日常使用中的语言都不可避免地发生变化。Megan Lukaniec 借助档案文献复兴温达特语（Wendat），她既感到要忠实于文献记录的压强，也拥有为这门语言开辟新路的自由。正在复兴沉睡的 myaamia 语的 Wesley Leonard 指出其中的讽刺：这些文献本身就是殖民权力的再次行使，宣称有权界定何为有效知识。"},{"en":"Standardizing documents can nevertheless help learning and teaching: programs such as the Kanyen’kéha school Onkwawenna Kentyohkwa use benchmarks like ACTFL’s Proficiency Guidelines as goals. Since learners differ in whether they want to read scholarly work, watch a film without subtitles, converse with relatives or pass a test, benchmarks may or may not help. Because you are the one doing the work, you decide what counts as proficient: if you can watch the film or talk with your aunties, you may call yourself proficient.","zh":"不过，标准化文件对学习与教学也可能有用：Kanyen’kéha 语的 Onkwawenna Kentyohkwa 学校等项目，就把 ACTFL 能力指南等基准作为学习者的目标。学习者的目的各不相同：读学术著作、看不带字幕的电影、与亲属交谈，或通过考试，因此基准可能有用，也可能无用。既然付出努力的是你自己，那么什么算熟练就由你决定：如果你已经能看懂那部电影，或能和姑姨们聊天，就可以称自己为熟练。"}]},"chapter-142-slug-12-4-cognitive-processes-in-language-learning":{"title":{"en":"12.4 Cognitive processes in language learning","zh":"12.4 语言学习中的认知过程"},"summary":{"en":"This section turns from social to psychological factors. A learner needs communicative input, and processing limits mean only part of it becomes intake; early grammars therefore rely heavily on content words, and sign learners make systematic handshape errors. Researchers distinguish declarative from procedural knowledge, and proficiency grows as processing becomes rapid and automatic through practice. It also introduces interlanguage and the interlanguage speech intelligibility benefit.","zh":"本节从社会因素转向心理因素。学习者需要具有交际性的输入，而加工能力的限制使其中只有一部分成为吸收；因此早期语法严重依赖实词，手语学习者的错误也集中在手形上。研究者区分陈述性知识与程序性知识，熟练度随加工经由练习变得快速自动化而提高。本节还介绍中介语以及中介语语音可懂度优势。"},"points":[{"en":"Language learning needs input that is used communicatively, linking forms with meaningful messages, not just abundant input.","zh":"语言学习需要用于交际的输入，把语言形式与有意义的信息联系起来，而不只是追求输入量。"},{"en":"Researchers contrast declarative knowledge, which is explicit, with procedural knowledge, which is unconscious.","zh":"研究者区分陈述性知识与程序性知识：前者是显性知识，后者是无意识的知识。"},{"en":"Attention and working memory are limited, so a learner’s intake is much smaller than the available input.","zh":"注意力与工作记忆有限，因此学习者的吸收量远小于可获得的输入量。"},{"en":"Early grammars are dominated by content words rather than function words or inflectional morphemes.","zh":"早期语法以实词为主，虚词和屈折语素所占比例较小。"},{"en":"Adult sign learners simplify systematically, most often in handshape and especially with two independent hands.","zh":"成年手语学习者会做系统性简化，最常出错的是手形，双手独立运动时尤为明显。"},{"en":"Interlanguage is the not-yet-fluent grammar of a learner, and it brings an intelligibility benefit among later learners.","zh":"中介语是学习者尚未流利的语法；它使后学语言者之间产生可懂度优势。"}],"terms":[{"en":"input","zh":"输入","defEn":"The language a learner hears, sees signed, or reads.","defZh":"学习者听到、看到手语或读到的语言材料。"},{"en":"intake","zh":"吸收（摄入）","defEn":"The portion of the input that the mind actually processes.","defZh":"输入中真正被头脑加工处理的那一部分。"},{"en":"declarative knowledge","zh":"陈述性知识","defEn":"Knowledge you know explicitly, such as your postal code.","defZh":"你能明确意识到的知识，例如自己的邮政编码。"},{"en":"procedural knowledge","zh":"程序性知识","defEn":"Unconscious knowledge that underlies skilled, automatic behaviour.","defZh":"支撑熟练自动化行为的无意识知识。"},{"en":"interlanguage","zh":"中介语","defEn":"A learner’s grammar that is not yet like an L1 user’s.","defZh":"学习者尚未达到母语者水平的语法系统。"},{"en":"intelligibility","zh":"可懂度","defEn":"How accurately listeners can identify what a talker said.","defZh":"听者能否准确辨认说话人所讲内容的程度。"}],"examples":[{"text":"a user of Auslan (Australian Sign Language) describing an event happening in Melbourne in January 2022","noteEn":"An unfamiliar signed sample that most learners cannot process much of.","noteZh":"大多数学习者无法有效加工的生疏手语样本。"},{"text":"a user of Kaurna (an Indigenous language of South Australia) introducing himself on the radio","noteEn":"An unfamiliar spoken sample where word boundaries are hard to find.","noteZh":"生疏的口语样本，连词与词的界限都难以辨认。"},{"text":"handshape","noteEn":"The usual locus of systematic articulation errors for adult sign learners.","noteZh":"成年手语学习者系统性发音错误最常见的位置。"},{"text":"interlanguage speech intelligibility benefit","noteEn":"Bent and Bradlow’s name for later learners being more intelligible to each other.","noteZh":"Bent 与 Bradlow 对后学语言者彼此更易听懂这一现象的命名。"}],"body":[{"en":"Earlier sections examined the social side of adult language learning; this one considers the psychological side. As in L1 acquisition, the goal is to construct a mental grammar, and one crucial ingredient is easily overlooked: learners need input, seeing the language signed or written or hearing it spoken. Input is only useful when it is used communicatively, so that the mind links the forms of the language with a meaningful message.","zh":"前面的小节考察了成人语言学习的社会面向，本节转向心理面向。与第一语言习得一样，目标是建构一套心理语法。有一个关键要素容易被忽视：学习者需要输入，要看到手语或书面语，或听到口语。只有用于交际时输入才有用，这样头脑才能把语言形式与有意义的信息联系起来。"},{"en":"Researchers debate whether the patterns of a later language come from overt instruction or are learned unconsciously, often contrasting declarative knowledge, which you know explicitly, such as your postal code, with procedural knowledge, which is unconscious and lets you recognize a sibling you have not seen in months. Either way, input helps only if the mind can process it, and beginners can attend to very little: confronted with Auslan or Kaurna, you may fail to recognize words or morphemes or even tell where words begin and end.","zh":"关于后学语言的规律来自显性教学还是无意识习得，研究者争论不休，并常把陈述性知识与程序性知识相对照：前者是你明确知道的东西，如邮政编码；后者是无意识的，让你能认出几个月未见的兄弟姐妹。无论哪种情况，输入只有在头脑能加工时才有用，而初学者能注意到的极少：面对 Auslan 或 Kaurna，你可能认不出词或语素，甚至分不清词与词的界限。"},{"en":"Because processing constraints limit intake, many early grammars consist disproportionately of content words rather than function words or inflectional morphemes, since the semantic content of nouns and verbs carries more crucial information than conjunctions or tense morphemes do. Processing limits also shape production: adults beginning to sign make systematic simplifications whose commonest errors are in handshape, especially in two-handed signs and most of all when the hands move independently.","zh":"由于加工限制压缩了吸收量，许多早期语法中实词的比例过高，虚词和屈折语素则偏少，因为在理解或表达某个想法时，名词和动词的语义内容比连词或时语素提供更关键的信息。加工限制也影响产出：成年人开始打手语时会出现系统性简化，最常见的错误在 handshape（手形），双手打出的手势尤其如此，两手独立运动时最为突出。"},{"en":"Gaining proficiency means moving from conscious, effortful processing to rapid, automatic processing, which takes a great deal of practice. There is also a period when you can produce and understand to some degree but your grammar still differs from an L1 user’s; this not-yet-fluent grammar is called interlanguage, and some researchers argue that interlanguages resemble each other regardless of your L1. Interlanguage also appears in accents: Bent and Bradlow found that adult learners of English from many L1 backgrounds were more intelligible to other later learners than L1 English talkers were.","zh":"提高熟练度意味着从有意识、费力的加工转向快速自动化的加工，而这需要大量练习。此外还有一段时期，你已具备一定的产出和理解能力，但语法仍与母语者相去甚远；这种尚未流利的语法称为中介语，一些研究者认为，无论第一语言是什么，中介语之间都有许多共同点。中介语也体现在口音上：Bent 与 Bradlow 发现，第一语言背景各异的英语后学语言者对其他后学语言者而言，比英语母语者更易听懂。"}]},"chapter-143-slug-12-5-your-l1-has-an-influence":{"title":{"en":"12.5 Learning a New Modality","zh":"12.5 学习一种新的模态"},"summary":{"en":"Unlike infants, adults already know at least one language, and that L1 grammar influences the grammar they are building, an effect called transfer, which can be positive or negative. When the new language also has a new modality, iconicity plays a role: it can ease learning when form resembles meaning, yet for adult sign learners it can also interfere, as when an iconic co-speech gesture competes with the actual sign.","zh":"与婴儿不同，成年人已经掌握至少一门语言，其第一语言的语法会影响正在建构的语法，这种效应称为迁移，可分为正迁移与负迁移。当所学语言还涉及新的模态时，象似性会起作用：形式与意义相似时可促进学习，但对成年手语学习者也可能造成干扰，例如象似性的伴随手势与真正的手势符号相互竞争。"},"points":[{"en":"A later learner already knows another language, so the L1 mental grammar influences the developing grammar.","zh":"后学语言者已掌握另一门语言，因此第一语言的心理语法会影响正在发展的语法。"},{"en":"Transfer is positive when L1 structures resemble the new language, making that part of learning easier.","zh":"当第一语言结构与新语言相似时，迁移为正迁移，使该部分学习更容易。"},{"en":"Negative transfer, or interference, occurs when L1 knowledge makes new structures harder to learn.","zh":"当第一语言知识使新结构更难学会时，出现负迁移，又称干扰。"},{"en":"Iconicity is more common in signed languages because the visual modality can represent meaning visually.","zh":"象似性在手语中更常见，因为视觉模态可以直接表现意义。"},{"en":"Adult BSL learners erred mainly in arbitrary handshape, almost never in the iconic location or orientation.","zh":"成年 BSL 学习者的错误主要出现在任意的词形手形上，几乎不出现在具有象似性的位置或朝向。"},{"en":"For the most complex signs, learners were less accurate with iconic signs than with arbitrary ones.","zh":"对最复杂的手势符号，学习者在象似性符号上的准确度反而低于任意性符号。"}],"terms":[{"en":"transfer","zh":"迁移","defEn":"Influence of the L1 mental grammar on a later language grammar.","defZh":"第一语言心理语法对后学语言语法的影响。"},{"en":"positive transfer","zh":"正迁移","defEn":"L1 knowledge that facilitates learning when structures are similar.","defZh":"当结构相似时，第一语言知识对学习起促进作用。"},{"en":"negative transfer","zh":"负迁移","defEn":"Interference in which L1 knowledge makes new structures harder.","defZh":"第一语言知识使新结构更难学习的干扰现象。"},{"en":"iconicity","zh":"象似性","defEn":"The similarity between the form of a word and its meaning.","defZh":"词的形式与意义之间的相似关系。"},{"en":"arbitrary","zh":"任意的","defEn":"Describing a form whose connection with meaning is not motivated.","defZh":"指形式与意义的联系没有理据。"},{"en":"reduplication","zh":"重叠","defEn":"Repetition of a form, here representing a repeated sound.","defZh":"形式的重复，在此象征声音的反复。"}],"examples":[{"text":"onion [ʌnjən] in English is Zwiebel [tsvibəl] in German and κρεμμύδι [kɾɛmydi] in Greek","noteEn":"Three words for the same vegetable whose forms are entirely arbitrary.","noteZh":"同一蔬菜的三个词形，其形式完全是任意的。"},{"text":"[koɾo]","noteEn":"A Japanese word for a small light object rolling in a single circle.","noteZh":"日语词，指小而轻的物体滚动一圈。"},{"text":"[ɡoɾogoɾo]","noteEn":"Voicing plus reduplication signals large irregular objects rolling continuously.","noteZh":"浊音化加重叠，表示一个或多个大的不规则物体不断滚动。"},{"text":"after seeing a video of the sign for WRITE","noteEn":"Learners used a writing gesture instead of imitating the BSL handshape.","noteZh":"学习者用写字的手势代替了模仿 BSL 的手形。"}],"body":[{"en":"Unlike an infant, an adult learning a later language already knows at least one other language, and the mental grammar of that L1 can influence the grammar being developed. This effect is called transfer. A structure in your L1 that resembles the one in your later language may produce positive transfer, facilitating learning; where the structures differ, negative transfer, also called interference, may make the new structures harder to learn.","zh":"与婴儿不同，成年后学习另一门语言时，你已经掌握至少一门别的语言，而这门第一语言的心理语法会影响正在发展的语法，这种效应称为迁移。第一语言中与后学语言相似的结构可能带来正迁移，促进学习；结构不同时，负迁移（也叫干扰）则可能使新结构更难学会。"},{"en":"The situation is especially interesting when the new language also has a new modality, for example when your L1 is spoken and the language you are learning is signed. Little transfer might be expected between the two grammars, yet iconicity appears to have both positive and negative transfer effects for adult learners of a signed language. A word’s iconicity has to do with the similarity between its form and its meaning. For many words the relation is entirely arbitrary: onion is [ʌnjən] in English, Zwiebel [tsvibəl] in German and κρεμμύδι [kɾɛmydi] in Greek.","zh":"当所学语言还涉及新的模态时，情况尤其有趣，例如第一语言是口语而所学的是手语。两套语法之间本来看似不会有太多迁移，但象似性对成年手语学习者似乎同时产生正、负两方面效应。词的象似性指形式与意义之间的相似程度。很多词的形式与意义完全任意：洋葱在英语中是 [ʌnjən]，德语中是 Zwiebel [tsvibəl]，希腊语中是 κρεμμύδι [kɾɛmydi]。"},{"en":"Some words, however, have an iconic relation to their meaning. In spoken languages iconicity appears in words referring to sounds, as in Japanese [koɾo] and [ɡoɾo], where reduplication iconically represents the repetition of the sound and the contrast between voiceless and voiced forms represents the difference between a small, pleasant sound and a loud, rumbly noise. Iconic forms are more common in signed languages because the visual modality can represent much of a word’s meaning visually, so the BSL, Turkish Sign Language (Türk İşaret Dili) and Icelandic Sign Language (Íslenskt táknmál) signs for beard all iconically represent a beard’s shape and location.","zh":"但有些词与意义存在象似关系。口语中象似性出现在指称声音的词里，例如日语 [koɾo] 与 [ɡoɾo]：重叠象征声音反复，清浊对立表现小而悦耳的声音与响亮低沉噪音之别。象似形式在手语中更常见，因为视觉模态能直接表现词义，因此英国手语（BSL）、土耳其手语（Türk İşaret Dili）和冰岛手语（Íslenskt táknmál）中表示胡须的手势都以象似方式表现胡须的形状与位置。"},{"en":"For fluent signers, high iconicity facilitates word recognition and production in ASL and BSL, but for later learners the effects are mixed. Marshall and Morgan asked adult BSL learners to describe scenarios in which two objects changed location, such as a ball moving from in front of a pen to behind it. The learners made many mistakes, mostly in handshape, an arbitrary component of the sign, and almost never in the location or orientation that iconically represent the objects. Ortega and Morgan, however, found that beginners imitating signs were less accurate with iconic words than arbitrary ones among the most complex signs, perhaps because a remembered iconic meaning drew attention from form, or an iconic gesture interfered.","zh":"对熟练的手语者来说，高象似性在 ASL 和 BSL 中都能促进词的识别与产出，但对后学语言者，效应则较为混杂。Marshall 与 Morgan 请成年 BSL 学习者描述两个物体改变位置的场景，例如球从笔前移到笔后。学习者的错误大多在 handshape（手形）这一任意成分上，几乎不出现在象似地表现物体位置与朝向的成分上。Ortega 与 Morgan 则发现，BSL 初学者模仿手势时，在最复杂的手势中，象似性符号的准确度低于任意性符号，这或许是因为记住的象似意义使注意偏离形式，也可能因为象似性的非语言手势造成干扰。"}]},"chapter-144-slug-12-6-learning-phonetics-and-phonotactics-in-a-later-language":{"title":{"en":"12.6 Learning Phonetics and Phonotactics in a Later Language","zh":"12.6 在后续语言中学习语音与音位配列"},"summary":{"en":"Adult learners already command the phonetic inventory and phonotactics of their first language, and these habits shape how they produce a later language. Unfamiliar segments tend to be replaced by familiar ones, and unfamiliar syllable shapes are repaired or avoided. Loanwords and foreign proper names show the same adaptation pressures.","zh":"成年学习者早已掌握第一语言的语音清单和音位配列，这些习惯会影响他们说后续语言的方式：不熟悉的音段容易被熟悉的音段替换，不合法的音节结构会被修补或回避。借词和外来专名的改造同样体现这种压力。"},"points":[{"en":"Adult learners substitute segments from their L1 inventory for sounds they have not yet learned to articulate.","zh":"成年学习者常用第一语言语音清单中的音段，替换自己尚未学会发音的音。"},{"en":"Phonotactic constraints restrict which sounds may appear in which positions and which syllable structures are legal.","zh":"音位配列制约限制哪些音能出现在哪些位置，以及哪些音节结构合法。"},{"en":"When a later language violates L1 syllable structure, learners repair the word shape to fit their grammar.","zh":"当后续语言的音节结构违反第一语言的规则时，学习者会改造词形以符合自己的语法。"},{"en":"Borrowed words undergo the same adaptation: epenthesis, substitution and resyllabification reshape them.","zh":"借词经历同样的改造：增音、替换和重新音节化都会重塑词形。"},{"en":"English speakers also adapt foreign proper names to English phonotactics, sometimes by deleting an illegal consonant.","zh":"英语使用者也会把外来专名改造成符合英语音位配列的形式，有时删除不合法的辅音。"}],"terms":[{"en":"phonetic inventory","zh":"语音清单","defEn":"The set of speech segments present in a grammar.","defZh":"某一语法中实际存在的全部语音音段的集合。"},{"en":"phonotactics","zh":"音位配列（语音组合法）","defEn":"Restrictions on what sounds may appear in what positions.","defZh":"对哪些音可以出现在哪些位置以及音节结构可能性的限制。"},{"en":"epenthesis","zh":"增音","defEn":"Inserting a segment to repair an illegal sound sequence.","defZh":"插入一个音段，使不合法的语音序列变得合法。"},{"en":"loanword","zh":"借词","defEn":"A word borrowed from one language into another.","defZh":"从一种语言借入另一种语言使用的词。"},{"en":"onset","zh":"音节首","defEn":"The consonant or consonants before the syllable nucleus.","defZh":"位于音节韵核之前的那个或那些辅音。"},{"en":"coda","zh":"韵尾","defEn":"The consonant or consonants after the syllable nucleus.","defZh":"位于音节韵核之后的那个或那些辅音。"}],"examples":[{"text":"Baruch [baɾʊx]","noteEn":"The Hebrew name ends in a velar fricative absent from English.","noteZh":"这个希伯来语名字以英语所没有的软腭擦音收尾。"},{"text":"Kavitha [kavit̪a]","noteEn":"The Tamil name has a dental stop in the last syllable onset.","noteZh":"这个泰米尔语名字的末音节首是一个齿塞音。"},{"text":"lung, tank, and singer","noteEn":"English velar nasal appears only in coda position.","noteZh":"英语的软腭鼻音只能出现在韵尾位置。"},{"text":"Nguyen [ŋwɪn]","noteEn":"Vietnamese allows the velar nasal in onset position.","noteZh":"越南语允许软腭鼻音出现在音节首位置。"}],"body":[{"en":"Speaking your first language gives you years of practice with the segments of its phonetic inventory, the set of segments present in the grammar. Most varieties of English have roughly 25 consonants and about a dozen vowels, a notably large vowel inventory that makes English vowels hard for adult learners. Other inventories differ strikingly: Hawaiian has just eight consonants and five vowels, while Adyghe has only three vowels but between 50 and 60 consonants. When learners meet a segment they have not learned to articulate, they often substitute a segment from their L1 inventory.","zh":"说第一语言的经历让你对其语音清单中的音段进行了长年练习，语音清单即语法中实际存在的音段集合。多数英语变体大约有 25 个辅音和十来个元音，元音数量偏多，使英语元音对成年学习者格外困难。其他语言的清单差别很大：夏威夷语只有 8 个辅音和 5 个元音，而阿迪格语只有 3 个元音，辅音却多达 50 至 60 个。当学习者遇到尚未学会发音的音段时，往往用第一语言清单中的音段来替换。"},{"en":"Phonotactic constraints in your L1 also shape production, because they restrict which sounds may occupy which positions and which syllable structures are possible. The velar nasal [ŋ] belongs to English but never appears in word onsets, only in codas such as lung, tank, and singer. Vietnamese also has the velar nasal, yet it is grammatical in onset position, as in the surname Nguyen [ŋwɪn]. Syllable structure is constrained too: English tolerates the complex clusters of strengths [strɛŋkθs] and also very simple syllables.","zh":"第一语言的音位配列制约同样影响发音，因为它限制哪些音可以占据哪些位置、哪些音节结构可以成立。软腭鼻音 [ŋ] 属于英语语音清单，却从不出现在词首，只能出现在 lung、tank 和 singer 这样的韵尾中。越南语也有软腭鼻音，但它可以合法地出现在音节首位置，如姓氏 Nguyen [ŋwɪn]。音节结构也受制约：英语既容许 strengths [strɛŋkθs] 这样复杂的辅音丛，也容许非常简单的音节。"},{"en":"Hawaiian shows how tight such constraints can be: a syllable may have at most one consonant in its onset, no coda consonants and no clusters. Borrowing the English word Christmas [krɪs.məs] therefore requires extensive repair. The consonant may appear only as a single onset, so [krɪ] becomes [kali], with [l] substituting for [r] and [i] for [ɪ]; the coda [s] gains a vowel and its own syllable to yield [ki]; and the [s] of the second syllable becomes another onset. The result is [kalikimaka].","zh":"夏威夷语显示这类制约可以多么严格：一个音节的首音最多只能有一个辅音，不能有韵尾辅音，也不能有辅音丛。因此借入英语词 Christmas [krɪs.məs] 需要大量改造。辅音只能作为单个音节首出现，于是 [krɪ] 变成 [kali]，其中 [l] 替换 [r]，[i] 替换 [ɪ]；韵尾 [s] 获得元音并自成音节，成为 [ki]；第二个音节的 [s] 则成为另一个音节首。最终结果是 [kalikimaka]。"},{"en":"Proper names are adapted in the same way. English speakers discussing the Polish city Gdańsk [ɡdaj̃sk] usually insert an extra [ə] between the first two consonants, since [ɡd] is not a legal English onset. When English borrows the German name Pfeiffer [pfaɪfɐ], the initial [p] is deleted instead, because [pf] cannot begin an English syllable.","zh":"专名的改造方式与此相同。英语使用者谈到波兰城市 Gdańsk [ɡdaj̃sk] 时，通常会在前两个辅音之间插入一个 [ə]，因为 [ɡd] 不是合法的英语音节首。英语借入德语名字 Pfeiffer [pfaɪfɐ] 时，词首的 [p] 反而被删除，因为 [pf] 不能充当英语音节的起始。"}]},"chapter-145-slug-12-7-learning-phonemes-and-allophones-in-a-later-language":{"title":{"en":"12.7 Learning Phonemes and Allophones in a Later Language","zh":"12.7 在后续语言中学习音位与音位变体"},"summary":{"en":"By twelve months of age infants have established the phoneme categories of their L1, so adult learners perceive a new language through those categories. The Perceptual Assimilation Model predicts which contrasts are easy and which are hard, depending on how new sounds map onto L1 phonemes. Zulu contrasts tested with English-speaking adults support these predictions.","zh":"婴儿在十二个月大时就已建立起第一语言的音位范畴，因此成年学习者会透过这些范畴去感知新语言。感知同化模型根据新语言语音如何映射到第一语音位来预测哪些对立容易学、哪些困难。用英语成年被试所做的祖鲁语对立实验结果支持这些预测。"},"points":[{"en":"Infants set up the phoneme categories of their L1 by about twelve months of age.","zh":"婴儿大约在十二个月大时便已建立第一语言的音位范畴。"},{"en":"Positive transfer occurs when a new contrast maps onto an existing contrast in the learner's L1.","zh":"当新语言的对立映射到学习者第一语言已有的对立时，就产生正迁移。"},{"en":"A new contrast should also be easy if the contrasting phones do not exist in the L1 at all.","zh":"如果新语言的几个对立音素在第一语言中完全不存在，这一对立同样应当容易学习。"},{"en":"Negative transfer arises when two contrasting phonemes of the later language map onto a single L1 phoneme.","zh":"当后续语言的两个对立音位映射到第一语言的同一个音位时，就会产生负迁移。"},{"en":"In the Zulu study, English listeners were highly accurate for voicing, moderately accurate for clicks and near chance for the implosive.","zh":"在祖鲁语研究中，英语听者对清浊对立准确率很高，对搭嘴音中等，对内爆音则接近随机水平。"}],"terms":[{"en":"Perceptual Assimilation Model","zh":"感知同化模型","defEn":"A theory predicting which non-native contrasts are difficult to discriminate.","defZh":"一种预测哪些非母语对立难以区分的理论。"},{"en":"positive transfer","zh":"正迁移","defEn":"L1 knowledge that helps rather than hinders later learning.","defZh":"第一语言知识对后续语言学习起促进而非阻碍作用。"},{"en":"negative transfer","zh":"负迁移","defEn":"L1 knowledge that interferes with learning a later language.","defZh":"第一语言知识对后续语言学习造成干扰。"},{"en":"phoneme category","zh":"音位范畴","defEn":"A mental category grouping sounds treated as the same segment.","defZh":"把若干听感上视为同一音段的音归为一类的心智范畴。"},{"en":"lateral fricative","zh":"边擦音","defEn":"A fricative produced with air flowing along the sides of the tongue.","defZh":"气流沿舌体两侧流出的擦音。"},{"en":"implosive","zh":"内爆音","defEn":"A stop released with air flowing into the mouth rather than out.","defZh":"除阻时气流向口内流入而非向口外流出的塞音。"}],"examples":[{"text":"voiced and voiceless lateral fricatives [ɬ and ɮ]","noteEn":"Zulu fricatives whose voicing contrast English listeners mapped easily.","noteZh":"祖鲁语中清浊相对的边擦音，英语听者能轻松映射其清浊对立。"},{"text":"a dental [ǀ], an alveolar [ǃ], and a palato-alveolar [ǂ] click","noteEn":"Three Zulu clicks that have no English counterpart at all.","noteZh":"祖鲁语的三种搭嘴音，在英语中完全不存在对应音。"},{"text":"The English adults were not much better than chance","noteEn":"Performance on the plosive and implosive bilabial stops.","noteZh":"英语成年人在双唇塞音与内爆音上的表现接近猜测水平。"},{"text":"The English listeners were about 95% correct","noteEn":"High accuracy for the voicing contrast between lateral fricatives.","noteZh":"对边擦音清浊对立的准确率很高，约为 95%。"}],"body":[{"en":"Babies have set up the phoneme categories of their first language by the time they are only twelve months old, so by adulthood those categories are deeply embedded in the mental grammar. Psycholinguist Catherine Best proposed the Perceptual Assimilation Model, which predicts which phoneme contrasts will be hard and which will be easy for adult learners; the theory centres on the concepts of phonemes and allophones.","zh":"婴儿在仅仅十二个月大时便已建立起第一语言的音位范畴，因此到了成年，这些范畴已深深嵌入心智语法。心理语言学家 Catherine Best 提出了感知同化模型，用以预测哪些音位对立对成年学习者困难、哪些容易；该理论的核心概念是音位和音位变体。"},{"en":"Best predicts positive transfer when a contrast in the new language maps onto a contrast already present in the learner's L1, which should make it easy to learn. She also predicts ease in the case of no transfer at all: if the new language has contrastive phones that do not exist in the L1, the learner can simply establish two new phoneme categories from scratch. Negative transfer arises when two contrasting phonemes of the later language map onto a single L1 phoneme category, because the learner has spent a lifetime treating the phonetic difference as mere allophonic variation rather than a meaningful contrast.","zh":"Best 预测，当新语言的对立映射到学习者第一语言中已有的对立时会出现正迁移，学习应当容易。她也预测完全无迁移的情形同样容易：如果新语言的对立音素在第一语言中根本不存在，学习者可以直接从零建立两个新的音位范畴。负迁移则出现在后续语言的两个对立音位映射到第一语言同一个音位范畴之时，因为学习者一生都把这种语音差异当作单纯的音位变体差异，而非有意义的对立。"},{"en":"Best and her colleagues tested the theory by investigating how English-speaking adults learn Zulu contrasts. English listeners were about 95% correct at distinguishing the voiced and voiceless lateral fricatives [ɬ and ɮ], since English has many fricative pairs contrasting in voicing, so the voicing difference mapped easily onto an existing contrast. They were about 80% correct on three Zulu clicks, a dental [ǀ], an alveolar [ǃ], and a palato-alveolar [ǂ] click; English has no clicks at all, so no L1 phonology interfered.","zh":"Best 及其同事通过考察说英语的成年人如何学习祖鲁语对立来检验该理论。英语听者区分清浊边擦音 [ɬ and ɮ] 的准确率约为 95%，因为英语中有大量以清浊相对立的擦音，清浊差异可以轻松映射到已有对立上。他们对三种祖鲁语搭嘴音——齿音 [ǀ]、齿龈音 [ǃ] 和腭龈音 [ǂ]——的准确率约为 80%；英语完全没有搭嘴音，因此没有第一语音系干扰。"},{"en":"The hardest case involved two kinds of bilabial stop: a plosive similar to English [b], and an implosive [ɓ] released with air flowing into the mouth. English adults were not much better than chance at hearing this difference. These results are consistent with the Perceptual Assimilation Model, since the listeners possess only one phoneme category for voiced bilabial stops, so their mental grammar treats the implosive as an allophone of the plosive.","zh":"最困难的情形涉及两类双唇塞音：一种是类似英语 [b] 的爆发音，另一种是除阻时气流向口内流入的内爆音 [ɓ]。英语成年人在分辨这一差异时并不比猜测好多少。这些结果与感知同化模型一致，因为听者对于浊双唇塞音只有一个音位范畴，其心智语法便把内爆音处理为爆发音的一个音位变体。"}]},"chapter-146-slug-12-7-exercise-your-linguistics-skills":{"title":{"en":"12.9 Exercise your linguistics skills","zh":"12.9 练习你的语言学技能"},"summary":{"en":"This section presents four open-ended exercises. The first two apply phonetic and phonotactic reasoning to French vowels and a German fricative contrast; the last two ask you to reflect on declarative versus procedural knowledge and on positive and negative transfer in your own language learning.","zh":"本节给出四道开放式练习。前两道把语音与音位配列的推理应用于法语元音和德语的擦音对立；后两道要求你反思陈述性知识与程序性知识的区别，以及自己语言学习中的正迁移与负迁移。"},"points":[{"en":"Exercise 1 asks which substitutions L1 English learners of French will make for the vowels [y] and [ʏ].","zh":"练习一要求判断以英语为第一语言的法语学习者会用哪些音替换元音 [y] 和 [ʏ]。"},{"en":"Exercise 2 asks how hard it is for an L1 English speaker to learn a German fricative contrast.","zh":"练习二询问以英语为母语者学习德语的擦音对立有多困难。"},{"en":"Exercise 3 asks you to sort your L1 knowledge into declarative and procedural knowledge, then compare a later language.","zh":"练习三要求把自己的第一语言知识分为陈述性知识与程序性知识，再与后续语言作比较。"},{"en":"Exercise 4 asks you to identify which parts of your L1 grammar produced positive or negative transfer.","zh":"练习四要求指出第一语言语法中哪些部分带来了正迁移或负迁移。"}],"terms":[{"en":"tense vowel","zh":"紧元音","defEn":"A vowel produced with relatively greater muscular tension and peripheral position.","defZh":"发音时肌肉较紧张、舌位较靠边缘的元音。"},{"en":"lax vowel","zh":"松元音","defEn":"A vowel produced with less muscular tension and a more central position.","defZh":"发音时肌肉较松弛、舌位较居中的元音。"},{"en":"declarative knowledge","zh":"陈述性知识","defEn":"Knowledge that something is the case, consciously available as facts.","defZh":"关于事实的知识，可以有意识地以命题形式提取。"},{"en":"procedural knowledge","zh":"程序性知识","defEn":"Knowledge of how to do something, typically used automatically.","defZh":"关于如何做某事的知识，通常自动化地加以运用。"},{"en":"negative transfer","zh":"负迁移","defEn":"Interference in later learning caused by earlier learned patterns.","defZh":"先前习得的模式对后续学习造成的干扰。"}],"examples":[{"text":"[lʏn]","noteEn":"A French word given as data for the lax high front rounded vowel.","noteZh":"作为松高前圆唇元音语料给出的法语词。"},{"text":"[tʀyke]","noteEn":"A French word given for the tense high front rounded vowel.","noteZh":"作为紧高前圆唇元音语料给出的法语词。"},{"text":"the voiceless post-alveolar fricative /ʃ/","noteEn":"The German phone said to contrast with another fricative phoneme.","noteZh":"德语中与另一个擦音音位形成对立的清龈后擦音。"},{"text":"voiceless velar fricative [x] and voiceless palatal fricative [ç]","noteEn":"Two allophones of the German phoneme posed in Exercise 2.","noteZh":"练习二中那个德语音位的两个音位变体。"}],"body":[{"en":"The first two exercises apply the phonetics and phonology of this chapter to new data. Exercise 1 supplies French words containing the tense and lax high, front, rounded vowels [y] and [ʏ], including [lʏn], [tʀʏk], [lynɛt] and [tʀyke]. Since neither vowel belongs to the English phonetic inventory, you must predict which English segments learners will substitute and justify your prediction. Exercise 2 concerns German, where the voiceless post-alveolar fricative /ʃ/ contrasts with a phoneme whose allophones are the voiceless velar fricative [x] and the voiceless palatal fricative [ç]; you must judge how difficult this contrast is for an L1 speaker of English.","zh":"前两道练习把本章的语音学与音系学知识应用于新的语料，要求你从语音清单和音位配列的角度作出预测并说明推理过程。练习一给出含紧、松高前圆唇元音 [y] 和 [ʏ] 的法语词，包括 [lʏn]、[tʀʏk]、[lynɛt] 和 [tʀyke]，两组词分别以松元音和紧元音出现。由于这两个元音都不属于英语的语音清单，你需要预测以英语为第一语言的学习者会替换成哪些英语音段，并说明你的预测依据。练习二涉及德语，其中清龈后擦音 /ʃ/ 与另一个音位形成对立，后者的音位变体是清软腭擦音 [x] 和清硬腭擦音 [ç]；你要结合英语音系的知识，判断这一对立对以英语为母语者究竟容易还是困难，并解释得出结论的方式。"},{"en":"The second pair of exercises turns to reflection on your own grammar. Exercise 3 asks you to examine your L1 mental grammar across phonetics and phonology, lexicon, morphology, syntax, semantics and pragmatics, decide which parts are declarative knowledge and which are more like procedural knowledge, and then ask whether your later-language knowledge should be classified in the same ways. Exercise 4 asks which parts of your L1 grammar produced positive transfer and which produced negative transfer, considering phonetics and phonology as well as morphology and syntax.","zh":"后两道练习转向对自己语法的反思，不提供额外数据，而是以你自己的语言经验为对象。练习三要求你审视第一语言的心智语法，涵盖语音与音系、词汇、形态、句法、语义和语用各个层面，判断哪些部分属于可以明确陈述的陈述性知识、哪些更像自动运行的程序性知识，进而思考你在后续语言中获得的语法知识是否应以同样方式分类，还是呈现出不同的分布。练习四则要求你回顾自己学习后续语言的经历，指出第一语言语法中哪些部分带来了正迁移、哪些部分造成了负迁移，并要同时考虑语音与音系以及形态和句法这两个方面。"}]}});
